.github.com/users/gigara/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wso2/product-integrator/commits/1e59bb52ef015c0ea8a10b2061d909ebb2215e4a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T04:42:57Z","email":"info@gigara.info","name":"gigara"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T08:49:08Z","email":"info@gigara.info","name":"gigara"},"message":"build(macos): drop the .pkg, and notarize the DMG that actually ships\n\nbuild.sh built an 838 MB .pkg per architecture that nothing ever published.\nThe DMG is assembled from the .app directly (`ditto \"$WSO2_TARGET/...\"` into\nthe staging dir), so the package was not an intermediate for it; the upload\nglob is `installers/mac/*.dmg` and `*-mac.zip`, and the v5.0.0 release assets\ncarry no .pkg. It was built, optionally signed, and deleted with the runner.\n\nIt was not merely wasted work. Notarization was gated on BOTH signing\nidentities, and the Developer ID Installer identity existed only to sign that\npackage — so on the first build to run with real certificates the gate took the\nskip path:\n\n    Imported certificates. App identity: Developer ID Application: WSO2, Inc. | Installer identity: none\n    [WARNING] MAC_INSTALLER_SIGNING_IDENTITY not set — .pkg will be unsigned (not notarizable)\n    Signing identities not available — skipping notarization (unsigned fallback build).\n\nA green build shipping a signed but un-notarized DMG, which every macOS 10.15+\nuser meets as \"Apple cannot check it for malicious software\". With the package\ngone the gate reduces to the Application identity, which is configured and\nworking, and the DMG is submitted and stapled.\n\nRemoving the .pkg orphans its resources: Distribution.xml, component.plist and\nthe welcome/conclusion/license files productbuild rendered. Deleted with it\n(the Apache text survives at the repo root). entitlements.plist and balscript\nstay — codesign and the DMG still use them. Also gone is the pair of in-place\n`sed -i ''''` edits that rewrote tracked Distribution.xml during a build and\nrestored it afterwards, leaving the tree dirty if anything failed between them.\n\nMACOS_INSTALLER_CERTIFICATE and MACOS_INSTALLER_CERTIFICATE_PASSWORD now have\nno consumer and can be deleted from the repository secrets.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4f610064ec3139934b1012a2774eba23dcae96ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wso2/product-integrator/git/trees/4f610064ec3139934b1012a2774eba23dcae96ad"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wso2/product-integrator/git/commits/1e59bb52ef015c0ea8a10b2061d909ebb2215e4a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16335290?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gigara","id":16335290,"login":"gigara","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MzM1Mjkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/wso2/