35290,"login":"gigara","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MzM1Mjkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wso2/product-integrator/commits/bfe0a5f6444c02c3d629e8e64f3cf3fc8b9772dc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T08:50:06Z","email":"info@gigara.info","name":"gigara"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T08:50:06Z","email":"info@gigara.info","name":"gigara"},"message":"ci: make the self-hosted k8s runner selectable alongside codebuild\n\ncompile.yml picked its Linux runner from a boolean `runOnAWS`, which can only\never express two choices. Replace it with the `runner` string the dispatchers\nalready collect, and resolve the label in `runs-on`: `codebuild` expands to the\nrun-scoped CodeBuild project name, and anything else — `ubuntu-latest`,\n`k8s-default-runners`, or a label added later — is used verbatim, so a new\nrunner needs no change here. `awsRunnerId` goes with it; nothing overrode it.\n\nThe free-disk-space step was gated on `!runOnAWS`, which would now also fire on\nthe self-hosted runner, where the action''s apt and docker reclaims assume a\nGitHub-hosted image. Gate it on `ubuntu-*` instead.\n\ndev-build.yml and release.yml offer `k8s-default-runners` in the dispatch\ndropdown; pr-ci.yml names `ubuntu-latest` in place of the dropped boolean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c231390788f78a95087493dbd5c9266d037c8a9e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wso2/product-integrator/git/trees/c231390788f78a95087493dbd5c9266d037c8a9e"},"url":"https://api.github.com