a5d33b51703d50e7","node_id":"C_kwDOPy5-RNoAKDIzYWY4MTVhNzZmNWY5YjZjYjcxMGIwZWE1ZDMzYjUxNzAzZDUwZTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/wso2/product-integrator/commit/e301d339ebad175fa202e1154f53dc0dab0d522f","sha":"e301d339ebad175fa202e1154f53dc0dab0d522f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wso2/product-integrator/commits/e301d339ebad175fa202e1154f53dc0dab0d522f"}],"sha":"23af815a76f5f9b6cb710b0ea5d33b51703d50e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wso2/product-integrator/commits/23af815a76f5f9b6cb710b0ea5d33b51703d50e7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16335290?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gigara","id":16335290,"login":"gigara","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MzM1Mjkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wso2/product-integrator/commits/9f729432ffc6919ccf91beec7c05ddc2cd1855a0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T09:20:46Z","email":"info@gigara.info","name":"gigara"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T09:20:46Z","email":"info@gigara.info","name":"gigara"},"message":"fix(update): refresh the repair claim''s mtime and re-check the marker before swapping (review)\n\nRound-3 review findings from NipunaRanasinghe on wso2/product-integrator#2467:\n\n- rename() keeps the renamed tree''s own mtime, so a `.repair-<pid>`\n  claim over a real (weeks-old) seed read as stale to the age guard\n  from the moment it existed — a concurrent sweep/GC could delete the\n  claimed tree in the claim-to-swap window, leaving the restore path\n  with nothing to rename back. The claim''s mtime is now refreshed with\n  utimes right after the rename (keeping, unlike a pid-only exemption\n  for .repair names, the reused-pid sweep after a crash+reboot). A\n  test documents the rename-keeps-mtime trap and the required refresh.\n\n- The swap re-checks the completion marker after copying: an instance\n  that spent minutes copying while a faster one completed the seed now\n  discards its own copy instead of pointlessly replacing a complete\n  tree through a brief no-target window. The swap comment now claims\n  only what the code enforces.\n\n- A failed adoption stamp is logged as an ERROR that names its real\n  cost (the containment walk repeats on every launch until the stamp\n  succeeds), not as an informational line.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c47100f5d94ebbd694f26ceb91635d91608bdb8c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wso2/product-integrator/git/trees/c47100f5d94ebbd694f26ceb91635d91608bdb8c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wso2/product-integrator/git/commits/9f729432ffc6919ccf91beec7c05ddc2cd1855a0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16335290?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gigara","id":16335290,"login":"gigara","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MzM1Mjkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/wso2/product-integrator/commit/9f729432ffc6919ccf91beec7c05ddc2cd1855a0","node_id":"C_kwDOPy5-RNoAKDlmNzI5NDMyZmZjNjkxOWNjZjkxYmVlYzdjMDVkZGMyY2QxODU1YTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/wso2/product-integrator/commit/614f1e075fa5552159882d9a9075ec2710fdd6b4","sha":"614f1e075fa5552159882d9a9075ec2710fdd6b4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wso2/product-integrator/commits/614f1e075fa5552159882d9a9075ec2710fdd6b4"}],"sha":"9f729432ffc6919ccf91beec7c05ddc2cd1855a0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wso2/product-integrator/commits/9f729432ffc6919ccf91beec7c05ddc2cd1855a0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16335290?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gigara","id":16335290,"login":"gigara","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MzM1Mjkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wso2/product-integrator/commits/614f1e075fa5552159882d9a9075ec2710fdd6b4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T08:40:55Z","email":"info@gigara.info","name":"gigara"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T08:40:55Z","email":"info@gigara.info","name":"gigara"},"message":"fix(update): adopt healthy marker-less seeds, copy-first swap, pid-reuse guard (review)\n\nReview findings from NipunaRanasinghe on wso2/product-integrator#2467:\n\n- Adopt-in-place: a marker-less target that still CONTAINS the bundled\n  payload (every source entry present with the same kind, no non-empty\n  source file empty in the target) gets its marker stamped in place\n  instead of being deleted and re-copied. Without this, every install\n  seeded before the marker existed would re-copy hundreds of MB\n  synchronously on the first launch after this ships, and a verified\n  updater download equal to the bundled version would be discarded.\n  Containment deliberately ignores extra entries, sizes and contents:\n  component homes mutate at runtime (ICP logs/database, the Ballerina\n  dependencies link), so equality checks would reject healthy seeds.\n\n- Copy first, swap after: the re-seed now stages the full replacement\n  before touching the existing tree, claims the old tree with an\n  atomic rename, and restores it if the swap fails. A copy failure\n  (disk full, antivirus handle) can no longer turn a present-but-\n  incomplete runtime into no runtime at all.\n\n- Pid-reuse guard: isActiveSeedingDir (nee isLiveSeedingDir) also\n  requires the staging/repair directory to be younger than a day, so a\n  pre-reboot leftover whose pid now names an unrelated live process is\n  swept instead of leaking forever (Windows recycles pids quickly).\n  The sweep and the component GC both use it.\n\n- The \"another instance completed first\" log line now includes the\n  underlying error, so a coinciding ENOSPC/EPERM is not masked as a\n  harmless race.\n\n- Tests for adoption, truncated-file rejection, keep-tree-on-failed-\n  re-seed (posix), aged-pid sweep, and the age+liveness helper. The GC\n  wiring itself is not testable from the node layer (the service\n  imports electron); the guard helper is covered directly.\n\n- WiX: SetWso2UserDataFolder moved Before=AppSearch — WixRemoveFoldersEx\n  is also scheduled after AppSearch, so the previous anchor left the\n  relative order to linker-assigned sequence numbers; if the reader ran\n  first, the property was empty and the cleanup silently did nothing.\n  Both gating properties arrive on the command line, so they are set\n  that early.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3869406fdcaf5406ce33aac3002640a33215a6ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wso2/product-integrator/git/trees/3869406fdcaf5406ce33aac3002640a33215a6ae"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wso2/product-integrator/git/commits/614f1e075fa5552159882d9a9075ec2710fdd6b4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16335290?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gigara","id":16335290,"login":"gigara","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MzM1Mjkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/wso2/product-integrator/commit/614f1e075fa5552159882d9a9075ec2710fdd6b4","node_id":"C_kwDOPy5-RNoAKDYxNGYxZTA3NWZhNTU1MjE1OTg4MmQ5YTkwNzVlYzI3MTBmZGQ2YjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/wso2/product-integrator/commit/dbf5af30a9ff62647b42e9aff306bde76c7dca2e","sha":"dbf5af30a9ff62647b42e9aff306bde76c7dca2e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wso2/product-integrator/commits/dbf5af30a9ff62647b42e9aff306bde76c7dca2e"}],"sha":"614f1e075fa5552159882d9a9075ec2710fdd6b4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wso2/product-integrator/commits/614f1e075fa5552159882d9a9075ec2710fdd6b4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16335290?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gigara","id":16335290,"login":"gigara","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MzM1Mjkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wso2/product-integrator/commits/dbf5af30a9ff62647b42e9aff306bde76c7dca2e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T08:18:04Z","email":"info@gigara.info","name":"gigara"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T08:18:04Z","email":"info@gigara.info","name":"gigara"},"message":"fix(update): claim partial seeds atomically before repair (review)\n\nReview findings from wso2/product-integrator#2467:\n\n- Repair now renames the marker-less target aside to a private\n  <target>.repair-<pid> name before deleting it. The rename is atomic,\n  so exactly one process wins the repair and a process stalled between\n  its marker check and its delete can no longer remove a target that a\n  faster instance completed in the meantime. Crashed repairs are swept\n  as stale (same pid-liveness rule as staging dirs) and the GC skips\n  live ones.\n\n- Corrected the durability comment on the seed marker: fsync makes the\n  marker itself torn-proof but does not make the copied payload\n  durable. The residual power-cut window is accepted deliberately —\n  per-file fsync stalls the first boot, and verifying payload stats on\n  later boots would false-positive and delete live data because\n  component homes mutate at runtime (ICP logs/database, the Ballerina\n  dependencies link).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9ec2aaa1515de417a7e51f752831b653c8e159fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wso2/product-integrator/git/trees/9ec2aaa1515de417a7e51f752831b653c8e159fe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wso2/product-integrator/git/commits/dbf5af30a9ff62647b42e9aff306bde76c7dca2e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16335290?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gigara","id":16335290,"login":"gigara","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MzM1Mjkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/wso2/product-integrator/commit/dbf5af30a9ff62647b42e9aff306bde76c7dca2e","node_id":"C_kwDOPy5-RNoAKGRiZjVhZjMwYTlmZjYyNjQ3YjQyZTlhZmYzMDZiZGU3NmM3ZGNhMmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/wso2/product-integrator/commit/23b9dced9224bbccbb37be898b49af8967d76c76","sha":"23b9dced9224bbccbb37be898b49af8967d76c76","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wso2/product-integrator/commits/23b9dced9224bbccbb37be898b49af8967d76c76"}],"sha":"dbf5af30a9ff62647b42e9aff306bde76c7dca2e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wso2/product-integrator/commits/dbf5af30a9ff62647b42e9aff306bde76c7dca2e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16335290?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gigara","id":16335290,"login":"gigara","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MzM1Mjkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wso2/product-integrator/commits/23b9dced9224bbccbb37be898b49af8967d76c76/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T06:12:18Z","email":"info@gigara.info","name":"gigara"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T06:12:18Z","email":"info@gigara.info","name":"gigara"},"message":"fix(update): heal partially seeded components and clean up user data on uninstall\n\nA fresh Windows install could end up with a permanently half-copied\ncomponent under ~/.wso2-integrator/components: first-run seeding runs\nbefore the single-instance lock, and two instances launched together\n(installer \"launch now\" + a shortcut double-click on the slow first\nboot) shared one staging directory. The second instance''s cleanup\ngutted the first one''s copy mid-flight, the first then renamed a tree\nwith holes into place, and the existence-only idempotence check\ntrusted it forever — reinstalling didn''t help; only manually deleting\nthe directory recovered the editor.\n\nSeeding changes (wso2ComponentUpdate.diff):\n- Per-pid staging (<version>.seeding-<pid>): racing instances can no\n  longer touch each other''s in-flight copy; the rename loser fails on\n  \"target exists\" and cleans up only its own directory.\n- A fsync''d .wso2-seeded marker is written last, and the skip check is\n  now target + marker: a marker-less directory (race commit, power\n  loss after the rename, or an already-broken seed in the field) is\n  deleted and re-seeded on the next launch, so affected machines\n  self-heal. When the bundled source is gone (editor-only install),\n  the partial tree is kept — it cannot be rebuilt.\n- Stale *.seeding* directories whose owning process is dead are swept.\n- The component GC now skips a live-pid seeding directory instead of\n  deleting a second instance''s copy in flight.\n- Unit tests for all of the above; fixed the latent -0 antisymmetry\n  assertion in the compareVersions test in passing.\n\nWindows MSI (installers/windows): a real uninstall now removes\n%USERPROFILE%\\.wso2-integrator via util:RemoveFolderEx so users don''t\nhave to find and delete the hidden folder by hand. The property is\nblank during major upgrades (UPGRADINGPRODUCTCODE) so app updates keep\nuser data, and `msiexec /x <msi> WSO2_KEEP_USERDATA=1` opts out.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"121d77608d5305838a2e3145482c8628aa6f775b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wso2/product-integrator/git/trees/121d77608d5305838a2e3145482c8628aa6f775b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wso2/product-integrator/git/commits/23b9dced9224bbccbb37be898b49af8967d76c76","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16335290?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gigara","id":16335290,"login":"gigara","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MzM1Mjkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/wso2/product-integrator/commit/23b9dced9224bbccbb37be898b49af8967d76c76","node_id":"C_kwDOPy5-RNoAKDIzYjlkY2VkOTIyNGJiY2NiYjM3YmU4OThiNDlhZjg5NjdkNzZjNzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/wso2/product-integrator/commit/e301d339ebad175fa202e1154f53dc0dab0d522f","sha":"e301d339ebad175fa202e1154f53dc0dab0d522f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wso2/product-integrator/commits/e301d339ebad175fa202e1154f53dc0dab0d522f"}],"sha":"23b9dced9224bbccbb37be898b49af8967d76c76","url":"https://api.githu