ved_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wso2/product-integrator/commits/8aa0a5a916b5f69940a98c351df3572d0e0750b6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T07:58:06Z","email":"info@gigara.info","name":"gigara"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T18:02:00Z","email":"nipunaranasinghe93@gmail.com","name":"NipunaRanasinghe"},"message":"fix(ci): require the update-bucket credentials in the publish preflight\n\nA release with AWS_UPDATE_S3_BUCKET set but no credentials — or the reverse —\nwould run the full macOS and Windows builds before anything noticed. The\npreflight already covers the bucket; the keys that write to it belong beside\nit.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n(cherry picked from commit 17bc1dd0b2de96b87fde6b3f90422f1776583ef0)","tree":{"sha":"9180cc03e82f1234effd5036d5b3309bb52d5876","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wso2/product-integrator/git/trees/9180cc03e82f1234effd5036d5b3309bb52d5876"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wso2/product-integrator/git/commits/8aa0a5a916b5f69940a98c351df3572d0e0750b6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29032600?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NipunaRanasinghe/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NipunaRanasinghe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NipunaRanasinghe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NipunaRanasinghe/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/NipunaRanasinghe","id":29032600,"login":"NipunaRanasinghe","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5MDMyNjAw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NipunaRanasinghe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NipunaRanasinghe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NipunaRanasinghe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NipunaRanasinghe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NipunaRanasinghe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NipunaRanasinghe","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/wso2/product-integrator/commit/8aa0a5a916b5f69940a98c351df3572d0e0750b6","node_id":"C_kwDOPy5-RNoAKDhhYTBhNWE5MTZiNWY2OTk0MGE5OGMzNTFkZjM1NzJkMGUwNzUwYjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/wso2/product-integrator/commit/704e26c193ac9d407d372adeb216202c0e215829","sha":"704e26c193ac9d407d372adeb216202c0e215829","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wso2/product-integrator/commits/704e26c193ac9d407d372adeb216202c0e215829"}],"sha":"8aa0a5a916b5f69940a98c351df3572d0e0750b6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wso2/product-integrator/commits/8aa0a5a916b5f69940a98c351df3572d0e0750b6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16335290?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gigara","id":16335290,"login":"gigara","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MzM1Mjkw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gigara","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wso2/product-integrator/commits/704e26c193ac9d407d372adeb216202c0e215829/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T06:38:40Z","email":"info@gigara.info","name":"gigara"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T18:02:00Z","email":"nipunaranasinghe93@gmail.com","name":"NipunaRanasinghe"},"message":"fix(ci): compare the pinned key against the signing key before the builds run\n\nChecking only that WSO2_UPDATE_PUBLIC_KEY is non-empty left the failure this\nchange is about — a pinned key from the wrong pair — to the late check in\nPublish Update Source, which runs after build-macos and build-windows have\nalready baked that key into product.json. Nothing downstream would catch it\neither: the signing steps verify against the signing key itself, so they pass.\n\nDerive and compare in resolve-versions instead. cosign-installer plus one\n`cosign public-key` costs seconds, and it also exercises COSIGN_PASSWORD, which\notherwise burns a full build before failing at the derive step. The late\ncomparison is now redundant and removed; Publish Update Source still derives\nsigning.pub for signature verification.\n\nAlso guard the decode with `[ -s pinned.pem ]` in both workflows — `base64 -d`\naccepts the empty string, so an empty secret used to skip the friendly error\nand die at openssl — and drop a comment left describing a `cosign.pub` write\nthat no longer exists.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n(cherry picked from commit f4fc335710cb21d96c71772859a4f757e2d0cf97)","tree":{"sha":"f5bb47f7aab5b1cba58054828c1c0daef90df8d8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wso2/product-integrator/git/trees/f5bb47f7aab5b1cba58054828c1c0daef90df8d8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wso2/product-integrator/git/commits/704e26c193ac9d407d372adeb216202c0e215829"