on-rpa/commit/f68cecaa3d3788fa924f3cfb0aacf7e436fd1c0d","sha":"f68cecaa3d3788fa924f3cfb0aacf7e436fd1c0d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iflytek/astron-rpa/commits/f68cecaa3d3788fa924f3cfb0aacf7e436fd1c0d"}],"sha":"df01ef0a6c013724967f1c4ef6c4d5c42b094010","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iflytek/astron-rpa/commits/df01ef0a6c013724967f1c4ef6c4d5c42b094010"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29982703?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bijinfeng/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bijinfeng/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bijinfeng/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bijinfeng/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bijinfeng","id":29982703,"login":"bijinfeng","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5OTgyNzAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bijinfeng/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bijinfeng/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bijinfeng/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bijinfeng/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bijinfeng/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bijinfeng","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iflytek/astron-rpa/commits/f68cecaa3d3788fa924f3cfb0aacf7e436fd1c0d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-02-10T07:30:08Z","email":"bijinfeng1016@gmail.com","name":"Kebai"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-02-10T07:30:08Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(i18n): add missing translations for smart component UI  (#529)\n\n* fix(i18n): add missing translations for smart component UI\n\n- Add English translations for smart component interface elements\n- Update configuration files for development environment and authentication\n- Fix grammar in English locale (\"Create an application\")\n- Replace hardcoded Chinese text with i18n keys across all smart component views\n- Ensure all UI strings are properly internationalized for English users\n\n* chore: update configuration and i18n for smart component assistant\n\n- Update remote address and authentication type in configuration\n- Add i18n translations for smart component assistant UI\n- Center-align prompt descriptions in UI\n- Refactor prompt items to be computed for reactivity\n- Replace hardcoded assistant title/subtitle with i18n keys\n- Add missing English translations for smart component feature\n\n* ci: use --no-frozen-lockfile for pnpm install in style check\n\nThis ensures the workflow can update the lockfile if needed, preventing potential failures when package versions in the lockfile conflict with those specified in package.json.\n\n* refactor(extension): encapsulate extensions in a manager class\n\nReplace mutable export with a singleton ExtensionManager to better control initialization and access. This prevents potential issues with accessing extensions before they are loaded.\n\nAdd eslint disable comment for the remaining mutable export in electron-app to suppress the warning, as it follows a different initialization pattern.","tree":{"sha":"689c4c17eb56d4d840f7f7233f0fc4beffc12a37","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iflytek/astron-rpa/git/trees/689c4c17eb56d4d840f7f7233f0fc4beffc12a37"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iflytek/astron-rpa/git/commits/f68cecaa3d3788fa924f3cfb0aacf7e436fd1c0d","verification":{"payload":"tree 689c4c17eb56d4d840f7f7233f0fc4beffc12a37\nparent 490b9fe6765d26311bd1c9a4123b3759929a0381\nauthor Kebai <bijinfeng1016@gmail.com> 1770708608 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1770708608 +0800\n\nfix(i18n): add missing translations for smart component UI  (#529)\n\n* fix(i18n): add missing translations for smart component UI\n\n- Add English translations for smart component interface elements\n- Update configuration files for development environment and authentication\n- Fix grammar in English locale (\"Create an application\")\n- Replace hardcoded Chinese text with i18n keys across all smart component views\n- Ensure all UI strings are properly internationalized for English users\n\n* chore: update configuration and i18n for smart component assistant\n\n- Update remote address and authentication type in configuration\n- Add i18n translations for smart component assistant UI\n- Center-align prompt descriptions in UI\n- Refactor prompt items to be computed for reactivity\n- Replace hardcoded assistant title/subtitle with i18n keys\n- Add missing English translations for smart component feature\n\n* ci: use --no-frozen-lockfile for pnpm install in style check\n\nThis ensures the workflow can update the lockfile if needed, preventing potential failures when package versions in the lockfile conflict with those specified in package.json.\n\n* refactor(extension): encapsulate extensions in a manager class\n\nReplace mutable export with a singleton ExtensionManager to better control initialization and access. This prevents potential issues with accessing extensions before they are loaded.\n\nAdd eslint disable comment for the remaining mutable export in electron-app to suppress the warning, as it follows a different initialization pattern.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpit6ACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9/gQADBxrR9tOGzknTF6gx5WxSPf\ng6BjCSR/xXHsQoohb807r5/RjKHFP6V6FGV7OHw4qP4kZBG2e7D/rbm3YIgyboua\nczSJL01r61gi6F0jVBRGzZ6l2cpTTLdKVmoke9FnWptest7J1oXW/aSPAZZ7yIGl\nlnmQckxOC8M9UlfJ0+o97R6YnYc060uSMMmKUurX13rEzAEHn8QDiqd+zHnLV3IK\nVInGc4GfXKS0IPdSnPSkWjNqvf4GXAEmLB2EkgEqasad5vvEpP5Ody8viwSUbDiL\nxRJX0zwuituhSW/lWUXI9JObY/ots9j8+h7u42PYYUaE2zLDfvjktiq0yDElBqm/\n03oEL21iIKzgjnkJ3EsH51xUOtZCzBIfqY5yqHoRyelx+qkv8UYh2xa62fWCzG5p\n11gOAmPbBTE9KajIVIBvI8Uu+9xgVYaTXYzT/UE+ung+/9Uu+0OEV2WGtfnOT1QS\nHA4jwvqUs6SIO5D9D2epqiEU8Op4VMoP2WOzEY0jp47BX2epFfrbsrFy7MvouLpp\nIrqVbyQcYJzfrtVuAYke6jQE6NLs/t0KvH+Ozbx480R7vdqaoZWrKt9uU5VdkxpB\nTmCzQVFwx3SmJ2FVyrAMGrOfF/DOmvc1Bl0tE5/GPtJj2Dk4MBYC/uOknEaNKd3X\ndMdAGbNwv5q2FUiUDMHd\n=0HTc\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-02-10T07:30:09Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/iflytek/astron-rpa/commit/f68cecaa3d3788fa924f3cfb0aacf7e436fd1c0d","node_id":"C_kwDOPzfEjNoAKGY2OGNlY2FhM2QzNzg4ZmE5MjRmM2NmYjBhYWNmN2U0MzZmZDFjMGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/iflytek/astron-rpa/commit/490b9fe6765d26311bd1c9a4123b3759929a0381","sha":"490b9fe6765d26311bd1c9a4123b3759929a0381","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iflytek/astron-rpa/commits/490b9fe6765d26311bd1c9a4123b3759929a0381"}],"sha":"f68cecaa3d3788fa924f3cfb0aacf7e436fd1c0d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iflytek/astron-rpa/commits/f68cecaa3d3788fa924f3cfb0aacf7e436fd1c0d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29982703?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bijinfeng/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bijinfeng/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bijinfeng/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bijinfeng/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bijinfeng","id":29982703,"login":"bijinfeng","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5OTgyNzAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bijinfeng/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bijinfeng/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bijinfeng/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bijinfeng/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bijinfeng/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bijinfeng","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iflytek/astron-rpa/commits/490b9fe6765d26311bd1c9a4123b3759929a0381/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-02-09T07:29:32Z","email":"bijinfeng1016@gmail.com","name":"Kebai"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-02-09T07:29:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Add plugin system with Module Federation support (#528)\n\n* Add plugin system with Module Federation support\n\nThis commit introduces a comprehensive plugin system using Module\nFederation for dynamic plugin loading. Key changes include:\n\n- Add new dependencies for plugin management including\n  @module-federation/enhanced, eventemitter3, and await-to-js\n- Remove casdoor-js-sdk dependency\n- Implement plugin context management with extension points for settings\n- Create plugin registry system for managing extensions and events\n- Add plugin manager with lifecycle methods for installation,\n  activation, and loading\n- Integrate plugin system with existing settings modal to support\n  plugin-provided settings tabs\n- Add Pinia store for plugin state management\n- Update vite-plugin-inspect to latest version for better compatibility\n\nThe plugin system supports dynamic loading of remote modules,\nactivation/deactivation lifecycle, and extensible contribution points\nfor adding functionality to the application.\n\n* Add RPA CLI package with basic command structure\n\n* Migrate from rslib to tsdown for build system\n\n- Replace rslib with tsdown in package.json scripts and dependencies\n- Remove rslib.config.ts files and add tsdown.config.ts files\n- Update TypeScript configuration for isolated declarations\n- Update pnpm-lock.yaml with tsdown dependencies\n\n* Refactor CLI implementation and add plugin demo\n\n- Switch from ESM to CommonJS output format\n- Add debug logging support and structured logger\n- Implement command structure with dev and build commands\n- Add utility functions for CLI argument parsing\n- Remove version constant in favor of package.json import\n- Add plugin demo package for testing CLI functionality\n\n* Add Vite build system to CLI and create plugin demo\n\n- Implement Vite-based dev server and build commands\n- Add module federation support for remote plugin exposure\n- Create plugin demo with Vue components and TypeScript config\n- Update dependencies to include Vite and related plugins\n\n* feat(plugins): implement extension system with module federation\n\n- Add plugin extension system with dynamic loading via module federation\n- Support plugin settings tabs registration in settings center\n- Implement plugin manager for loading, activating, and managing plugins\n- Add custom protocol handler for extension resource loading in electron\n- Remove deprecated plugin store and migrate to new extension system\n- Update module federation dependencies to latest versions\n- Configure electron build to include extensions directory\n\n* refactor(extension): switch from package.json to mf-manifest.json for plugin config\n\n- Update plugin manager to remove hardcoded ''module'' type when registering remotes\n- Modify Vite build config to set publicPath for module federation manifest\n- Rewrite extension initialization to read from mf-manifest.json instead of package.json\n- Change from synchronous file operations to async/await with error handling\n- Update manifest structure to use metaData.buildInfo.buildVersion and publicPath\n\n* feat(cli): add config system for module federation\n\nIntroduce defineConfig and loadRpaConfig utilities to allow projects to customize federation configuration. The system automatically loads rpa.config.* files and merges user configuration with defaults, enabling custom remote names and shared dependencies.\n\n* feat(cli): support async config functions and overload signatures\n\nAdd support for asynchronous configuration functions and promise-based configs in defineConfig. This allows users to dynamically generate configuration based on environment variables and other runtime conditions.\n\n* feat(cli): add plugin template creation command and Vue template\n\n- Add `rpa create` command to scaffold new plugin projects with interactive prompts\n- Include Vue-based template with TypeScript, RPA configuration, and example plugin\n- Conditionally set publicPath in dev mode to support local development\n- Remove debug console log from electron protocol handler\n- Add required dependencies for template rendering and CLI prompts\n\n* docs(cli): add English and Chinese README files\n\nAdd comprehensive README documentation for the CLI package, covering installation, usage, commands, and development instructions in both English and Chinese locales.\n\n* build: upgrade @module-federation/enhanced from ^0.24.0 to ^2.0.0\n\nUpdate the dependency version in package.json and reflect the change in pnpm-lock.yaml. This major version upgrade may include breaking changes, so the lockfile has been updated accordingly to ensure consistent installation across environments.\n\n* chore: update remote address and authentication type\n\n- Change remote_addr from dev.iflyrpa.private to 172.29.231.250 for connectivity\n- Switch app_auth_type from uap to casdoor for authentication method update\n\n* fix: remove redundant process.exit calls in CLI commands\n\n- Remove process.exit calls after cancel calls to prevent double exit\n- Use cancel function which already handles exit logic appropriately\n- Ensure consistent error handling flow in CLI command execution","tree":{"sha":"6bb5f5a61fde32367c51c0c48c51b55e79499bd5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iflytek/astron-rpa/git/trees/6bb5f5a61fde32367c51c0c48c51b55e79499bd5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iflytek/astron-rpa/git/commits/490b9fe6765d26311bd1c9a4123b3759929a0381","verification":{"payload":"tree 6bb5f5a61fde32367c51c0c48c51b55e79499bd5\nparent ca7fd104c610665f9de9668279470d756956ffd3\nauthor Kebai <bijinfeng1016@gmail.com> 1770622172 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1770622172 +0000\n\nfeat: Add plugin system with Module Federation support (#528)\n\n* Add plugin system with Module Federation support\n\nThis commit introduces a comprehensive plugin system using Module\nFederation for dynamic plugin loading. Key changes include:\n\n- Add new dependencies for plugin management including\n  @module-federation/enhanced, eventemitter3, and await-to-js\n- Remove casdoor-js-sdk dependency\n- Implement plugin context management with extension points for settings\n- Create plugin registry system for managing extensions and events\n- Add plugin manager with lifecycle methods for installation,\n  activation, and loading\n- Integrate plugin system with existing settings modal to support\n  plugin-provided settings tabs\n- Add Pinia store for plugin state management\n- Update vite-plugin-inspect to latest version for better compatibility\n\nThe plugin system supports dynamic loading of remote modules,\nactivation/deactivation lifecycle, and extensible contribution points\nfor adding functionality to the application.\n\n* Add RPA CLI package with basic command structure\n\n* Migrate from rslib to tsdown for build system\n\n- Replace rslib with tsdown in package.json scripts and dependencies\n- Remove rslib.config.ts files and add tsdown.config.ts files\n- Update TypeScript configuration for isolated declarations\n- Update pnpm-lock.yaml with tsdown dependencies\n\n* Refactor CLI implementation and add plugin demo\n\n- Switch from ESM to CommonJS output format\n- Add debug logging support and structured logger\n- Implement command structure with dev and build commands\n- Add utility functions for CLI argument parsing\n- Remove version constant in favor of package.json import\n- Add plugin demo package for testing CLI functionality\n\n* Add Vite build system to CLI and create plugin demo\n\n- Implement Vite-based dev server and build commands\n- Add module federation support for remote plugin exposure\n- Create plugin demo with Vue components and TypeScript config\n- Update dependencies to include Vite and related plugins\n\n* feat(plugins): implement extension system with module federation\n\n- Add plugin extension system with dynamic loading via module federation\n- Support plugin settings tabs registration in settings center\n- Implement plugin manager for loading, activating, and managing plugins\n- Add custom protocol handler for extension resource loading in electron\n- Remove deprecated plugin store and migrate to new extension system\n- Update module federation dependencies to latest versions\n- Configure electron build to include extensions directory\n\n* refactor(extension): switch from package.json to mf-manifest.json for plugin config\n\n- Update plugin manager to remove hardcoded ''module'' type when registering remotes\n- Modify Vite build config to set publicPath for module federation manifest\n- Rewrite extension initialization to read from mf-manifest.json instead of package.json\n- Change from synchronous file operations to async/await with error handling\n- Update manifest structure to use metaData.buildInfo.buildVersion and publicPath\n\n* feat(cli): add config system for module federation\n\nIntroduce defineConfig and loadRpaConfig utilities to allow projects to customize federation configuration. The system automatically loads rpa.config.* files and merges user configuration with defaults, enabling custom remote names and shared dependencies.\n\n* feat(cli): support async config functions and overload signatures\n\nAdd support for asynchronous configuration functions and promise-based configs in defineConfig. This allows users to dynamically generate configuration based on environment variables and other runtime conditions.\n\n* feat(cli): add plugin template creation command and Vue template\n\n- Add `rpa create` command to scaffold new plugin projects with interactive prompts\n- Include Vue-based template with TypeScript, RPA configuration, and example plugin\n- Conditionally set publicPath in dev mode to support local development\n- Remove debug console log from electron protocol handler\n- Add required dependencies for template rendering and CLI prompts\n\n* docs(cli): add English and Chinese README files\n\nAdd comprehensive README documentation for the CLI package, covering installation, usage, commands, and development instructions in both English and Chinese locales.\n\n* build: upgrade @module-federation/enhanced from ^0.24.0 to ^2.0.0\n\nUpdate the dependency version in package.json and reflect the change in pnpm-lock.yaml. This major version upgrade may include breaking changes, so the lockfile has been updated accordingly to ensure consistent installation across environments.\n\n* chore: update remote address and authentication type\n\n- Change remote_addr from dev.iflyrpa.private to 172.29.231.250 for connectivity\n- Switch app_auth_type from uap to casdoor for authentication method update\n\n* fix: remove redundant process.exit calls in CLI commands\n\n- Remove process.exit calls after cancel calls to prevent double exit\n- Use cancel function which already handles exit logic appropriately\n- Ensure consistent error handling flow in CLI command execution","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP S