feat(docker): add new environment variables and enhance MySQL initialization scripts\n\n- Added CUA_BASE_URL and CUA_API_KEY to the .env.example file.\n- Updated docker-compose.yml to include a new SQL initialization script for c_atom_meta.\n- Enhanced MySQL initialization scripts by adding TRUNCATE statements for various tables to ensure clean data loading.\n\nThese changes improve the configuration and data management for the Docker setup.\n\nSigned-off-by: doctorbruce <benyouyou2000@hotmail.com>\n\n* fix(schema): set default value for deleted column in MySQL and HCL files\n\n- Updated the `deleted` column in both MySQL schema.sql and HCL schema.hcl to set a default value of 0, ensuring consistent behavior for logical deletion across different database implementations.\n\nSigned-off-by: doctorbruce <benyouyou2000@hotmail.com>\n\n* refactor: update build and docker configurations\n\n- Modified `build.bat` to include a custom PyPI index for package installation.\n- Removed the `init_c_atom_meta_data.sql` initialization script from `docker-compose.yml` to streamline database setup.\n- Deleted the `c_atom_meta` table definition from `schema.sql` and updated the `c_atom_meta_new` table definition to reflect changes in the database schema.\n- Adjusted the initialization script for `c_atom_meta_new` to ensure proper data loading.\n\nThese changes enhance the build process and improve the clarity of the database schema.\n\nSigned-off-by: doctorbruce <benyouyou2000@hotmail.com>\n\n* feat(sql): update slider_hover initialization for web element interaction\n\n- Enhanced the `slider_hover` entry in the `init_c_atom_meta_new_data.sql` file to improve the functionality for web element interaction, including detailed input parameters for browser object, slider element, progress element, drag direction, and duration.\n\nThese changes aim to provide a more comprehensive setup for handling slider interactions in web automation tasks.\n\nSigned-off-by: doctorbruce <benyouyou2000@ho