i.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/narrowstacks/dorkroom/commit/5f0d061e036da6356b8dee7f1f3e2b71c7f8b194","node_id":"C_kwDOP0YsJdoAKDVmMGQwNjFlMDM2ZGE2MzU2YjhkZWU3ZjFmM2UyYjcxYzdmOGIxOTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/narrowstacks/dorkroom/commit/fa5749f59b19ad34f5a729578c2a0af4917a4d64","sha":"fa5749f59b19ad34f5a729578c2a0af4917a4d64","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/narrowstacks/dorkroom/commits/fa5749f59b19ad34f5a729578c2a0af4917a4d64"}],"sha":"5f0d061e036da6356b8dee7f1f3e2b71c7f8b194","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/narrowstacks/dorkroom/commits/5f0d061e036da6356b8dee7f1f3e2b71c7f8b194"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2106980?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/narrowstacks","id":2106980,"login":"narrowstacks","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMDY5ODA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/narrowstacks/dorkroom/commits/fa5749f59b19ad34f5a729578c2a0af4917a4d64/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T01:21:53Z","email":"aaron@affords.art","name":"aaron f.a"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T01:21:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(films): stop eagerly fetching lazy-loaded thumbnails on /films (#361)\n\n* fix(films): stop eagerly fetching thumbnails, defeating loading=lazy\n\nisImageCached() constructed a probe Image and assigned src to it from the\nuseState initializer on every FilmImage render (and again on src change),\nwhich started a real download for every rendered card, overscan included,\nregardless of loading=\"lazy\" on the actual <img>.\n\nReplace the probe with a ref on the real <img>, checked in a layout effect\nafter mount (img.complete && naturalWidth > 0) plus the existing\nonLoad/onError, so an already-cached image skips the skeleton without any\nextra fetch. Keep the module-level loadedImageCache Set to avoid a flash on\nremount (e.g. scrolling a virtualized list); it''s now only ever populated by\nonLoad or the complete check, never by a probe.\n\nAlso add decoding=\"async\" and explicit width/height (matching sizeMap) on\nthe real <img>, and a loading prop (default ''lazy'', override ''eager'' for the\ndetail panel''s hero image, which is guaranteed to be in the viewport as soon\nas it mounts).\n\nPart of #353\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(films): keep the timed-out thumbnail''s <img> mounted for a late load\n\nReview fixes for #353:\n\n- The 5s \"give up\" timeout unmounted the real <img> (via showFallback),\n  which cancels any pending lazy-loaded fetch and removes the onLoad handler\n  that could have recovered it. With loading=\"lazy\", the browser can defer a\n  fetch well past 5s (e.g. Safari not extending the lazy margin into a\n  nested overflow scroller), so a since-completed load was lost for good.\n  Now only !src/hasError unmount the <img>; a timeout instead overlays the\n  fallback icon on top of the still-mounted (opacity-0) <img>, and a late\n  onLoad clears hasTimedOut to swap the real image back in.\n- Rewrote the \"cached image\" test to use an http(s) src with\n  HTMLImageElement.prototype complete/naturalWidth stubbed via\n  Object.defineProperty (restored in afterEach), instead of a data: URL that\n  happy-dom decodes for real regardless of the complete-check under test.\n  Added the complete=true/naturalWidth=0 case to prove the skeleton stays.\n- The window.Image spy test called through to happy-dom''s real constructor,\n  which throws \"Illegal constructor\"; give it a safe mockImplementation and\n  add vi.restoreAllMocks()/vi.useRealTimers() to afterEach so mocks don''t\n  leak into later tests.\n- Added a fake-timers test: advance 5000ms -> fallback icon shown, <img>\n  still mounted; fireEvent.load -> icon gone, image visible.\n- Wrapped the multi-card render in a <div> instead of a Fragment\n  (biome noUselessFragments).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"471c4433b56cff73b11629ab68f1e79489629b8d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/narrowstacks/dorkroom/git/trees/471c4433b56cff73b11629ab68f1e79489629b8d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/narrowstacks/dorkroom/git/commits/fa5749f59b19ad34f5a729578c2a0af4917a4d64","verification":{"payload":"tree 471c4433b56cff73b11629ab68f1e79489629b8d\nparent 3b74d10d4812daa1998ed92528f1df525c4c138c\nauthor aaron f.a <aaron@affords.art> 1790126513 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790126513 -0700\n\nfix(films): stop eagerly fetching lazy-loaded thumbnails on /films (#361)\n\n* fix(films): stop eagerly fetching thumbnails, defeating loading=lazy\n\nisImageCached() constructed a probe Image and assigned src to it from the\nuseState initializer on every FilmImage render (and again on src change),\nwhich started a real download for every rendered card, overscan included,\nregardless of loading=\"lazy\" on the actual <img>.\n\nReplace the probe with a ref on the real <img>, checked in a layout effect\nafter mount (img.complete && naturalWidth > 0) plus the existing\nonLoad/onError, so an already-cached image skips the skeleton without any\nextra fetch. Keep the module-level loadedImageCache Set to avoid a flash on\nremount (e.g. scrolling a virtualized list); it''s now only ever populated by\nonLoad or the complete check, never by a probe.\n\nAlso add decoding=\"async\" and explicit width/height (matching sizeMap) on\nthe real <img>, and a loading prop (default ''lazy'', override ''eager'' for the\ndetail panel''s hero image, which is guaranteed to be in the viewport as soon\nas it mounts).\n\nPart of #353\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(films): keep the timed-out thumbnail''s <img> mounted for a late load\n\nReview fixes for #353:\n\n- The 5s \"give up\" timeout unmounted the real <img> (via showFallback),\n  which cancels any pending lazy-loaded fetch and removes the onLoad handler\n  that could have recovered it. With loading=\"lazy\", the browser can defer a\n  fetch well past 5s (e.g. Safari not extending the lazy margin into a\n  nested overflow scroller), so a since-completed load was lost for good.\n  Now only !src/hasError unmount the <img>; a timeout instead overlays the\n  fallback icon on top of the still-mounted (opacity-0) <img>, and a late\n  onLoad clears hasTimedOut to swap the real image back in.\n- Rewrote the \"cached image\" test to use an http(s) src with\n  HTMLImageElement.prototype complete/naturalWidth stubbed via\n  Object.defineProperty (restored in afterEach), instead of a data: URL that\n  happy-dom decodes for real regardless of the complete-check under test.\n  Added the complete=true/naturalWidth=0 case to prove the skeleton stays.\n- The window.Image spy test called through to happy-dom''s real constructor,\n  which throws \"Illegal constructor\"; give it a safe mockImplementation and\n  add vi.restoreAllMocks()/vi.useRealTimers() to afterEach so mocks don''t\n  leak into later tests.\n- Added a fake-timers test: advance 5000ms -> fallback icon shown, <img>\n  still mounted; fireEvent.load -> icon gone, image visible.\n- Wrapped the multi-card render in a <div> instead of a Fragment\n  (biome noUselessFragments).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsymxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAd74QAC0VkXGEu5R800lTykmrYzGK\nu9+bHd4rEhG3GhwVvMhV+w0G7bVquJik0Aw4o0M/kVX/D5bUW0ZmzaI53ILuGbPu\n4dwMB3rS1IfbUrffyBBUXaySC9bwyn9E6p3fEYsR6xqvMyx3sGBk/a2e0oEby2nn\na3N7i/dgHBVQPzLqofvpIikji/3DxL5SUantgOG/OL2O/5afFSn0903/tAvMLGzJ\nVlOREKImMycVpfiWIHcXuRWCcINbu43I2MI9IA14Nixg+23s1RZEiBo0HP1IX/CI\nOPTMQD8BZqA71NXrrEpCXGVUpGA3lNl2DsCMUvccQCXD3H1YMUYYUcmzj5yXelfG\n74hqyS1aYbyQqFhR7KyazAxILREHS9SGbuWgdju0No6uNY8RdAYQIdycLYQvFFGl\nVIwWpM5DEG900TW5H3lxVo3mAl+vRZiu7TioJGq1XnB4uUUpRLdX83MMy1FRFBdW\n0gCn60KXD/kKUFpQd2XWsBfUUeSPjOVdeh9uT6i+SIJJA+AxZXnyXVzbcFaZml2K\nhWZj/PfJEG8aHtTWTPWT8IZ31QJYgqfevpjKKAJ2sDayf272t+HZYBMJQ/n6ByiK\nQZuqpKpyXg+vDi7NEGaQp0uzjB7TcqAZVG35P9ymD+7+eQkP+orQ7403ycpBaNLo\n1mWwPZhGlGdjympFoP45\n=3PGr\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-23T01:21:54Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/narrowstacks/dorkroom/commit/fa5749f59b19ad34f5a729578c2a0af4917a4d64","node_id":"C_kwDOP0YsJdoAKGZhNTc0OWY1OWIxOWFkMzRmNWE3Mjk1NzhjMmEwYWY0OTE3YTRkNjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/narrowstacks/dorkroom/commit/3b74d10d4812daa1998ed92528f1df525c4c138c","sha":"3b74d10d4812daa1998ed92528f1df525c4c138c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/narrowstacks/dorkroom/commits/3b74d10d4812daa1998ed92528f1df525c4c138c"}],"sha":"fa5749f59b19ad34f5a729578c2a0af4917a4d64","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/narrowstacks/dorkroom/commits/fa5749f59b19ad34f5a729578c2a0af4917a4d64"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2106980?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/narrowstacks","id":2106980,"login":"narrowstacks","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMDY5ODA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/narrowstacks/dorkroom/commits/3b74d10d4812daa1998ed92528f1df525c4c138c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T01:21:46Z","email":"aaron@affords.art","name":"aaron f.a"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T01:21:46Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(exposure): warn when an EV preset needs a value beyond the dial range (#360)\n\n* fix(exposure): warn when an EV preset needs a value beyond the dial range\n\napplyPreset solved the free variable and snapped it with findNearestStandard,\nwhich silently returned the endpoint (30s, f/64, ...) when the solution fell\noutside the standard range, landing the exposure several stops from the\npreset''s EV with no indication.\n\nAdd presetWarning to useCameraExposureCalculator: set when the snapped value\nis more than 1/3 stop from the exact solved value, cleared on any input\nchange or a subsequent in-range preset. The web page surfaces it as an\ninline StatusAlert notice near the EV result.\n\nFixes #337\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(exposure): correct preset warning direction, aperture stop size, and a11y\n\nAddresses review feedback on the #337 fix:\n\n- PresetWarning now carries a direction (''over'' | ''under'', derived from\n  solved vs. the snapped standard value) so the hint and \"beyond the limit\"\n  wording match which way the preset missed. The too-bright aperture case\n  (1/30, ISO 12800, EV 16) previously told the user to open the aperture\n  further, which was backwards; it now suggests a faster shutter, lower\n  ISO, or an ND filter.\n- getPresetOutOfRangeWarning weights aperture stops by 2x the raw log2\n  distance, since an f-number stop is a factor of sqrt(2), not 2.\n- formatISO clamps to a minimum of 1 so an extremely bright ISO solve can''t\n  render as \"ISO 0\"; a dedicated aperture formatter rounds large required\n  values to a whole f-stop (f/529) instead of one decimal place (f/528.8).\n- PresetWarningNotice now renders a persistent <output aria-live=\"polite\">\n  wrapper (present even with no warning) so screen readers announce the\n  first warning, not just later swaps. StatusAlert gained an `omitRole`\n  prop to avoid nesting two live regions.\n- Added getPresetOutOfRangeWarning unit tests (tolerance boundary, the\n  aperture 2x weighting, the NaN/non-positive guard, both directions), an\n  ISO-mode hook test, a solveFor-clears-warning hook test, and a page test\n  asserting the too-bright aperture hint never says to open the aperture.\n\nPart of #337\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(exposure): stop applyPreset from reading a stale values closure\n\nCodex flagged (PR #360, comment 4077635729) that applyPreset read `values`\nfrom the render closure to compute the warning. Calling set() then\napplyPreset() in the same handler — exactly what the hook''s own JSDoc\nexample does — solved the preset against the previous render''s settings\ninstead of the value set() had just committed.\n\napplyPreset is back to a pure functional setValues(prev => ...) updater,\nas it was before the presetWarning feature, with no side effects inside it\n(StrictMode double-invokes updaters). It now only records the applied\npreset''s EV (lastPresetEv), separately, once. presetWarning is derived via\nuseMemo from lastPresetEv plus the committed values: since only the\nsolved-for field changes when a preset applies, re-solving from the\ncurrent (post-set) other two fields reproduces the same result applyPreset\nused to pick `nearest`.\n\nAdded a regression test: set(''aperture'', 5.6) then applyPreset(-2) in one\nact() must solve from f/5.6 (needs ~125.4s), not the stale f/8 default\n(which would need 256s, the original #337 example).\n\nPart of #337\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"27096ecc311928e87695331c79fea433deebeeaf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/narrowstacks/dorkroom/git/trees/27096ecc311928e87695331c79fea433deebeeaf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/narrowstacks/dorkroom/git/commits/3b74d10d4812daa1998ed92528f1df525c4c138c","verification":{"payload":"tree 27096ecc311928e87695331c79fea433deebeeaf\nparent 3ec827a8a33d440d1fd3cb028ca579e200535d88\nauthor aaron f.a <aaron@affords.art> 1790126506 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790126506 -0700\n\nfix(exposure): warn when an EV preset needs a value beyond the dial range (#360)\n\n* fix(exposure): warn when an EV preset needs a value beyond the dial range\n\napplyPreset solved the free variable and snapped it with findNearestStandard,\nwhich silently returned the endpoint (30s, f/64, ...) when the solution fell\noutside the standard range, landing the exposure several stops from the\npreset''s EV with no indication.\n\nAdd presetWarning to useCameraExposureCalculator: set when the snapped value\nis more than 1/3 stop from the exact solved value, cleared on any input\nchange or a subsequent in-range preset. The web page surfaces it as an\ninline StatusAlert notice near the EV result.\n\nFixes #337\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(exposure): correct preset warning direction, aperture stop size, and a11y\n\nAddresses review feedback on the #337 fix:\n\n- PresetWarning now carries a direction (''over'' | ''under'', derived from\n  solved vs. the snapped standard value) so the hint and \"beyond the limit\"\n  wording match which way the preset missed. The too-bright aperture case\n  (1/30, ISO 12800, EV 16) previously told the user to open the aperture\n  further, which was backwards; it now suggests a faster shutter, lower\n  ISO, or an ND filter.\n- getPresetOutOfRangeWarning weights aperture stops by 2x the raw log2\n  distance, since an f-number stop is a factor of sqrt(2), not 2.\n- formatISO clamps to a minimum of 1 so an extremely bright ISO solve can''t\n  render as \"ISO 0\"; a dedicated aperture formatter rounds large required\n  values to a whole f-stop (f/529) instead of one decimal place (f/528.8).\n- PresetWarningNotice now renders a persistent <output aria-live=\"polite\">\n  wrapper (present even with no warning) so screen readers announce the\n  first warning, not just later swaps. StatusAlert gained an `omitRole`\n  prop to avoid nesting two live regions.\n- Added getPresetOutOfRangeWarning unit tests (tolerance boundary, the\n  aperture 2x weighting, the NaN/non-positive guard, both directions), an\n  ISO-mode hook test, a solveFor-clears-warning hook test, and a page test\n  asserting the too-bright aperture hint never says to open the aperture.\n\nPart of #337\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(exposure): stop applyPreset from reading a stale values closure\n\nCodex flagged (PR #360, comment 4077635729) that applyPreset read `values`\nfrom the render closure to compute the warning. Calling set() then\napplyPreset() in the same handler — exactly what the hook''s own JSDoc\nexample does — solved the preset against the previous render''s settings\ninstead of the value set() had just committed.\n\napplyPreset is back to a pure functional setValues(prev => ...) updater,\nas it was before the presetWarning feature, with no side effects inside it\n(StrictMode double-invokes updaters). It now only records the applied\npreset''s EV (lastPresetEv), separately, once. presetWarning is derived via\nuseMemo from lastPresetEv plus the committed values: since only the\nsolved-for field changes when a preset applies, re-solving from the\ncurrent (post-set) other two fields reproduces the same result applyPreset\nused to pick `nearest`.\n\nAdded a regression test: set(''aperture'', 5.6) then applyPreset(-2) in one\nact() must solve from f/5.6 (needs ~125.4s), not the stale f/8 default\n(which would need 256s, the original #337 example).\n\nPart of #337\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsymqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAkHEQAGQ5f9vXvYQTvc8OmC/piK/6\nk3qd0RU7PwkIYx8cNzN9R646EooMGCHqlnYXvC5JsRyIqEusUtQah2CTMNuxnNRC\n9ydwcELdOMIYCgs5g43hrwJ23O2D3tTU0I0EmKEEw7rXwAd1hODI8GHejp6QEoB8\n6fAHlCpPLvOPyyZhwk3or+87K81VBtaZ96oaNA0u3qTyqTymtIiaw6BHnc2wMTTQ\n1lOqJ49VrbtONIdET+Yegn2YfO3NB1ywrSKGvl67AD/2aD4W6LoJT+eIZNcfrro3\ntTaK3VEksGA6G1ALpaJHceabndp4paO1a397fs9lztgxRMmDPy1xWnn5UhS4ex0n\nEG/2lZJM/n9l+/cLNr4jK9JDRHU3D++3lIeag0MV/J8G5g7MX4T2QBE7wPGRFQnS\nbiZX8O+TkDyFhaBRFBN2z3s+NTleamnoZqtpuzR9d2jJL7v9xE5osMoM1/M8/JSu\nrGg753ZpZr9RMXUu4+gnufILymjLxilLAzdtOfwM9ngJdzQyLmjP7JJcqIE4xxsj\nJ95cMh0Kal354yD8Hyyia+lbhVVK1tkU6ztafpgzSa+sFOGbibdF0U/ye/5deCwG\naz9VK6Md/wqqF+lRI1S2MdXvtk2wcXKkqOZIrtSzEwNiReKqzkbMG+Qfl5c/lw1U\nVkY3OXuB/Uuzy6uSjhxs\n=m9br\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-23T01:21:46Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/narrowstacks/dorkroom/commit/3b74d10d4812daa1998ed92528f1df525c4c138c","node_id":"C_kwDOP0YsJdoAKDNiNzRkMTBkNDgxMmRhYTE5OThlZDkyNTI4ZjFkZjUyNWM0YzEzOGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/narrowstacks/dorkroom/commit/3ec827a8a33d440d1fd3cb028ca579e200535d88","sha":"3ec827a8a33d440d1fd3cb028ca579e200535d88","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/narrowstacks/dorkroom/commits/3ec827a8a33d440d1fd3cb028ca579e200535d88"}],"sha":"3b74d10d4812daa1998ed92528f1df525c4c138c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/narrowstacks/dorkroom/commits/3b74d10d4812daa1998ed92528f1df525c4c138c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2106980?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/narrowstacks","id":2106980,"login":"narrowstacks","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMDY5ODA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/narrowstacks/dorkroom/commits/3ec827a8a33d440d1fd3cb028ca579e200535d88/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T01:21:38Z","email":"aaron@affords.art","name":"aaron f.a"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T01:21:38Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(mobile-nav): reserve bottom space so the floating toggle can''t overlap page content (#359)\n\n* fix(mobile-nav): reserve bottom space so the floating toggle can''t overlap page content\n\nThe fixed mobile-nav toggle (bottom-right, size-12, sm:hidden) sat on top of\nwhatever a route rendered last on phones — e.g. the right-aligned \"Next\"\npagination button on /development — so tapping it opened the nav drawer\ninstead. `<main>` in __root.tsx now reserves\n`calc(env(safe-area-inset-bottom)+5rem)` of bottom padding below sm, removed\nat sm+ where the toggle is hidden.\n\nhome-page and lens-calculator-page already carried their own unconditional\npb-24/pb-16 for bottom whitespace; gated those to sm+ so mobile doesn''t get\ndouble padding on top of main''s new reservation.\n\nFixes #345\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(border): stop the mobile border layout''s background seam under the FAB reservation\n\n/border at mobile width showed a two-tone seam: mobile-border-layout.tsx''s\nmin-h-dvh + explicit `background: var(--color-background)` were added\ndeliberately (b121a0b) to paint a solid surface over the app''s decorative\nbackdrop-gradient, so they''re kept rather than dropped. Its own pb-24 then\nstacked with __root.tsx''s new bottom reservation (#345), leaving that strip\nuncovered by this div''s background and showing the gradient through.\nReplaced pb-24 with a negative margin-bottom of the same amount main reserves\nplus a larger padding-bottom, so the extra padding''s background bleeds into\nthe reserved strip instead of adding a second gap.\n\nAlso added a comment at mobile-nav.tsx''s FAB pointing back to the 5rem\nreservation in __root.tsx, so resizing the button and updating the\nreservation stay in sync.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c4ff1d3e67164d9aceb5a82522ece43647a54d6b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/narrowstacks/dorkroom/git/trees/c4ff1d3e67164d9aceb5a82522ece43647a54d6b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/narrowstacks/dorkroom/git/commits/3ec827a8a33d440d1fd3cb028ca579e200535d88","verification":{"payload":"tree c4ff1d3e67164d9aceb5a82522ece43647a54d6b\nparent 7354dd6ec0c9c94ad9b2e0d3042e33d352eedb1f\nauthor aaron f.a <aaron@affords.art> 1790126498 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790126498 -0700\n\nfix(mobile-nav): reserve bottom space so the floating toggle can''t overlap page content (#359)\n\n* fix(mobile-nav): reserve bottom space so the floating toggle can''t overlap page content\n\nThe fixed mobile-nav toggle (bottom-right, size-12, sm:hidden) sat on top of\nwhatever a route rendered last on phones — e.g. the right-aligned \"Next\"\npagination button on /development — so tapping it opened the nav drawer\ninstead. `<main>` in __root.tsx now reserves\n`calc(env(safe-area-inset-bottom)+5rem)` of bottom padding below sm, removed\nat sm+ where the toggle is hidden.\n\nhome-page and lens-calculator-page already carried their own unconditional\npb-24/pb-16 for bottom whitespace; gated those to sm+ so mobile doesn''t get\ndouble padding on top of main''s new reservation.\n\nFixes #345\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(border): stop the mobile border layout''s background seam under the FAB reservation\n\n/border at mobile width showed a two-tone seam: mobile-border-layout.tsx''s\nmin-h-dvh + explicit `background: var(--color-background)` were added\ndeliberately (b121a0b) to paint a solid surface over the app''s decorative\nbackdrop-gradient, so they''re kept rather than dropped. Its own pb-24 then\nstacked with __root.tsx''s new bottom reservation (#345), leaving that strip\nuncovered by this div''s background and showing the gradient through.\nReplaced pb-24 with a negative margin-bottom of the same amount main reserves\nplus a larger padding-bottom, so the extra padding''s background bleeds into\nthe reserved strip instead of adding a second gap.\n\nAlso added a comment at mobile-nav.tsx''s FAB pointing back to the 5rem\nreservation in __root.tsx, so resizing the button and updating the\nreservation stay in sync.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsymiCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAHdUQACDV4R480eOHrTt8yAJD6OLb\n27UsQ9lLFx4gwzsQ53Jznu6nmljlhHHOJ2gdSUFLZ5m2D0FGx7qiRpRct8bVleNB\nKoH2zmf7bjj6DCI/bXmIwXJqj9ToqY/JS/v9pXSzyUSraqpaY2wTW75cjwYxTJyt\n7pzh1MJicE4VPt4tya6n9P8kxt049gZn7iGN16PpzyaCdMtXHnOJYymxs1aMGGMm\nqRzD8Ft1ylUJnmoUYdFy7tObva3LpbckNhxBB9LNdrfaQHFrjprBYpNaHyOkrHT2\nvL9POkoXG3UvcnK1zCgjWM7sNorzLaXFwVMnQY5BT3qAGBkHduHpYkUTC6GcNYxz\nBFcC2PCp38NHKQX1MnHzfsH3gU5JQdLefsDoDLDPJYfSBWe/lO8kQKLgvef4lZId\nwYagWsHGOst0PTzBHS3QEPEltBC63T3IHmeLOPtaXK2YZdV/zL17sx20b1g7aDP1\nfDoVdAiTQXyTMCvF7RzxMRRI417ZXRMY+6K/EVdd1TO0G+xvnnyAu6z9OawswkPz\nR09nwxoYx5DDecn36IjUC0xHmKyxL3pV30t/brFK0QJzyGhGAlKFw2jn/xc3jYvq\no0P4wnLAJXaQWGtMeRl/Lq9cfxIFeRonT+mLUae45DFqrqafeGjiUhEl8zh4bp1n\nEE6diZ4J8v+fAtvdhH5U\n=stxM\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-23T01:21:39Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/narrowstacks/dorkroom/commit/3ec827a8a33d440d1fd3cb028ca579e200535d88","node_id":"C_kwDOP0YsJdoAKDNlYzgyN2E4YTMzZDQ0MGQxZmQzY2IwMjhjYTU3OWUyMDA1MzVkODg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/narrowstacks/dorkroom/commit/7354dd6ec0c9c94ad9b2e0d3042e33d352eedb1f","sha":"7354dd6ec0c9c94ad9b2e0d3042e33d352eedb1f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/narrowstacks/dorkroom/commits/7354dd6ec0c9c94ad9b2e0d3042e33d352eedb1f"}],"sha":"3ec827a8a33d440d1fd3cb028ca579e200535d88","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/narrowstacks/dorkroom/commits/3ec827a8a33d440d1fd3cb028ca579e200535d88"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2106980?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/narrowstacks","id":2106980,"login":"narrowstacks","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMDY5ODA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/narrowstacks/dorkroom/commits/7354dd6ec0c9c94ad9b2e0d3042e33d352eedb1f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T01:21:30Z","email":"aaron@affords.art","name":"aaron f.a"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T01:21:30Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(routing): show the styled error UI for route render errors (#357)\n\n* fix(routing): show the styled error UI for route render errors\n\nTanStack Router''s own global CatchBoundary was catching route render\nerrors before the app-level ErrorBoundary around <RouterProvider> ever\nsaw them, so users got an unstyled \"Something went wrong!\" box with the\nheader/nav gone, and app_error never fired.\n\nWire defaultErrorComponent/defaultOnCatch on createRouter instead: each\nmatched route gets its own boundary scoped to that route''s slot, so the\nroot layout survives and the existing @dorkroom/ui fallback (now split\nout as ErrorFallback) renders in its place, with a Try Again button that\ncalls router.invalidate(). defaultOnCatch reports app_error exactly once,\nmirroring the outer boundary''s onError.\n\nAlso fix vite:preloadError calling preventDefault() even when the 10s\nreload guard skips the reload, which silently swallowed the chunk error\ninstead of letting it surface.\n\nFixes #330\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(routing): address review on route error UI (#330)\n\nAddresses PR review feedback on the route-error-component work:\n\n- ErrorFallback now supports a secondaryAction button. RouteErrorComponent\n  offers both \"Try Again\" (router.invalidate()) and \"Reload Page\"\n  (window.location.reload()), since React.lazy caches a rejected dynamic\n  import permanently — a retry alone can never recover from a stale chunk.\n  A chunk-load-shaped error message promotes Reload Page to primary.\n- Fixed the message/button mismatch: ErrorFallback takes a `message` prop,\n  and RouteErrorComponent passes neutral copy that fits either action.\n- Reworded the route-error-component.tsx comment: the outer ErrorBoundary\n  also only ever sees errors from outside the router, or thrown by the\n  error component itself — not root-route render errors, which get the\n  same defaultErrorComponent/defaultOnCatch as every other route.\n- Extracted defaultErrorComponent/defaultOnCatch into an exported\n  `routeErrorOptions` (apps/dorkroom/src/app/lib/route-error-options.ts,\n  kept out of route-error-component.tsx so it stays a components-only file\n  for react-doctor''s only-export-components rule), spread into createRouter\n  in main.tsx and imported by the test, so deleting it from main.tsx would\n  fail the test rather than staying green.\n- defaultOnCatch now skips trackEvent when a preload reload was just\n  triggered (wasRecentPreloadReload(), reading preload-error-recovery.ts''s\n  guard key), so a stale-chunk error about to be fixed by that reload\n  doesn''t get counted as app_error. Repeated \"Try Again\" clicks on a\n  genuine, deterministic render error still re-report app_error each time;\n  documented as accepted, no dedupe.\n- Added role=\"alert\" and heading focus-on-mount to ErrorFallback, and the\n  packages/ui/CLAUDE.md focus-visible ring to its buttons.\n- preload-error-recovery.ts: wrapped sessionStorage get/set in try/catch;\n  on failure it neither reloads nor calls preventDefault().\n- Tests: a rejecting React.lazy() route now covers the Reload Page action;\n  preload-error-recovery tests cover the storage-unavailable path and\n  wasRecentPreloadReload, with useRealTimers() moved to afterEach.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(routing): fix incorrect example in route-error-component comment\n\nThe outer ErrorBoundary comment cited \"a bug in __root.tsx''s own render\"\nas an example error it still catches, but the root match gets the same\ndefaultErrorComponent/defaultOnCatch as every other route, so that never\nreaches it either. Point at what actually can: a provider wrapping\n<RouterProvider>, or the <Analytics> component next to it. Also note that\na root-route render error still goes through this same boundary, just\nwithout a surviving header.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(routing): address Codex review comments on #330\n\nThree P1s from the Codex bot on PR #357:\n\n- Root CLAUDE.md rule 5 forbids \"error\"/\"warning\" in file names. Renamed\n  the five new files and their exports for consistency:\n  preload-error-recovery.(ts|test.ts) -> preload-chunk-recovery.(ts|test.ts),\n  route-error-options.ts -> route-fallback-options.ts (routeErrorOptions ->\n  routeFallbackOptions), route-error-component.(tsx|test.tsx) ->\n  route-fallback.(tsx|test.tsx) (RouteErrorComponent -> RouteFallback).\n  The pre-existing packages/ui/src/components/error-boundary.tsx is\n  untouched by this rule (not a new file).\n- Added an optional `className` to ErrorFallbackProps, merged onto the\n  wrapper `<div>` via `cn()`, per packages/ui/CLAUDE.md''s \"accept an\n  optional className prop for overrides\" convention.\n- Changed the fallback''s two buttons from `rounded-lg` to `rounded-xl`,\n  matching packages/ui/CLAUDE.md''s radius scale (buttons -> rounded-xl).\n  The dev-only raw-error `<pre>` block isn''t a button, so it keeps\n  `rounded-lg`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2726825e475775e26f8e617cd4029947204740bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/narrowstacks/dorkroom/git/trees/2726825e475775e26f8e617cd4029947204740bd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/narrowstacks/dorkroom/git/commits/7354dd6ec0c9c94ad9b2e0d3042e33d352eedb1f","verification":{"payload":"tree 2726825e475775e26f8e617cd4029947204740bd\nparent bb6d51ac140b8018a8b4a0e28f1f9c0b16e0f3ca\nauthor aaron f.a <aaron@affords.art> 1790126490 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790126490 -0700\n\nfix(routing): show the styled error UI for route render errors (#357)\n\n* fix(routing): show the styled error UI for route render errors\n\nTanStack Router''s own global CatchBoundary was catching route render\nerrors before the app-level ErrorBoundary around <RouterProvider> ever\nsaw them, so users got an unstyled \"Something went wrong!\" box with the\nheader/nav gone, and app_error never fired.\n\nWire defaultErrorComponent/defaultOnCatch on createRouter instead: each\nmatched route gets its own boundary scoped to that route''s slot, so the\nroot layout survives and the existing @dorkroom/ui fallback (now split\nout as ErrorFallback) renders in its place, with a Try Again button that\ncalls router.invalidate(). defaultOnCatch reports app_error exactly once,\nmirroring the outer boundary''s onError.\n\nAlso fix vite:preloadError calling preventDefault() even when the 10s\nreload guard skips the reload, which silently swallowed the chunk error\ninstead of letting it surface.\n\nFixes #330\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(routing): address review on route error UI (#330)\n\nAddresses PR review feedback on the route-error-component work:\n\n- ErrorFallback now supports a secondaryAction button. RouteErrorComponent\n  offers both \"Try Again\" (router.invalidate()) and \"Reload Page\"\n  (window.location.reload()), since React.lazy caches a rejected dynamic\n  import permanently — a retry alone can never recover from a stale chunk.\n  A chunk-load-shaped error message promotes Reload Page to primary.\n- Fixed the message/button mismatch: ErrorFallback takes a `message` prop,\n  and RouteErrorComponent passes neutral copy that fits either action.\n- Reworded the route-error-component.tsx comment: the outer ErrorBoundary\n  also only ever sees errors from outside the router, or thrown by the\n  error component itself — not root-route render errors, which get the\n  same defaultErrorComponent/defaultOnCatch as every other route.\n- Extracted defaultErrorComponent/defaultOnCatch into an exported\n  `routeErrorOptions` (apps/dorkroom/src/app/lib/route-error-options.ts,\n  kept out of route-error-component.tsx so it stays a components-only file\n  for react-doctor''s only-export-components rule), spread into createRouter\n  in main.tsx and imported by the test, so deleting it from main.tsx would\n  fail the test rather than staying green.\n- defaultOnCatch now skips trackEvent when a preload reload was just\n  triggered (wasRecentPreloadReload(), reading preload-error-recovery.ts''s\n  guard key), so a stale-chunk error about to be fixed by that reload\n  doesn''t get counted as app_error. Repeated \"Try Again\" clicks on a\n  genuine, deterministic render error still re-report app_error each time;\n  documented as accepted, no dedupe.\n- Added role=\"alert\" and heading focus-on-mount to ErrorFallback, and the\n  packages/ui/CLAUDE.md focus-visible ring to its buttons.\n- preload-error-recovery.ts: wrapped sessionStorage get/set in try/catch;\n  on failure it neither reloads nor calls preventDefault().\n- Tests: a rejecting React.lazy() route now covers the Reload Page action;\n  preload-error-recovery tests cover the storage-unavailable path and\n  wasRecentPreloadReload, with useRealTimers() moved to afterEach.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(routing): fix incorrect example in route-error-component comment\n\nThe outer ErrorBoundary comment cited \"a bug in __root.tsx''s own render\"\nas an example error it still catches, but the root match gets the same\ndefaultErrorComponent/defaultOnCatch as every other route, so that never\nreaches it either. Point at what actually can: a provider wrapping\n<RouterProvider>, or the <Analytics> component next to it. Also note that\na root-route render error still goes through this same boundary, just\nwithout a surviving header.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(routing): address Codex review comments on #330\n\nThree P1s from the Codex bot on PR #357:\n\n- Root CLAUDE.md rule 5 forbids \"error\"/\"warning\" in file names. Renamed\n  the five new files and their exports for consistency:\n  preload-error-recovery.(ts|test.ts) -> preload-chunk-recovery.(ts|test.ts),\n  route-error-options.ts -> route-fallback-options.ts (routeErrorOptions ->\n  routeFallbackOptions), route-error-component.(tsx|test.tsx) ->\n  route-fallback.(tsx|test.tsx) (RouteErrorComponent -> RouteFallback).\n  The pre-existing packages/ui/src/components/error-boundary.tsx is\n  untouched by this rule (not a new file).\n- Added an optional `className` to ErrorFallbackProps, merged onto the\n  wrapper `<div>` via `cn()`, per packages/ui/CLAUDE.md''s \"accept an\n  optional className prop for overrides\" convention.\n- Changed the fallback''s two buttons from `rounded-lg` to `rounded-xl`,\n  matching packages/ui/CLAUDE.md''s radius scale (buttons -> rounded-xl).\n  The dev-only raw-error `<pre>` block isn''t a button, so it keeps\n  `rounded-lg`.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsymaCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA1mkQAEprpKg4BiBtnC4R5gKueYbG\nBulVfMzOE8CTjr2ajuLdCiHAgkst18FFPmODvjVWakRn/Xuyagb+CaXU/xcAwPGb\nMuQ3JT8pVyO0vzIT/noDNn0zEGxsbFopfqJCiJz7sSDPme6GyRaAre8jhaE6Z+sV\nA4SIQlYKy7CJbXHAJw6lw+TqDxEiXTlAzlLBmOv37LrOZpSVzSwM9b2MesY7D9YX\n81PWPkbpnain2kSoNZ+UIC9k58gn2zkrbxgBrTS1PrgM0lXfZAuIZlhATPxrZpH8\n4l/CLfFAw5f+oCeQ0WiJndQqxNO+5rGVvCP9lOuMa4a9CAu3uyYyfFbB/96/wHMM\naRWjE6QMWjfCH9eYq83p6MPVxR4vS8oemzALbGW87niX5AqN2bB2vj3WQbEpd2zO\nBpVY89sOk9pqMp+mPI25yoxOGxWviPKZ5S+h5U6l9QLUQGInYMx+zImzU23fm8To\n6JvQutXyqv28LQNLJFIVKvkms/khtO3LPAiXdFt/wf/HgS7rDhn8rYtJcoFwRMhf\nTuiFMDCFFkzeEzzL5zgO3z9Mj7MA8cQJ3SQmFq5m8TpECjznFIdjTIW3655SNkLj\n8cChKh8RFt6/OzpBCw61FAhFoQIHm6Vc4nlPJOGewEBlYczDuLg3AeS5SO0TjOLr\nz6/R2DZHISacTIFu49as\n=364r\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-23T01:21:31Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api