ca"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2106980?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/narrowstacks","id":2106980,"login":"narrowstacks","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMDY5ODA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/narrowstacks/dorkroom/commits/3a1c9618425e2bb5712efaacf5bd117bfe7dd096/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T23:46:27Z","email":"aaron@affords.art","name":"aaron f.a"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T23:46:27Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(mat): follow the global imperial/metric preference (#315)\n\n* feat(mat): follow the global imperial/metric preference\n\nThe mat calculator never read `useMeasurement()`, so a metric user got\ncentimetres on /border and /resize but fractional inches on /mat.\n\nForm state, presets, persistence and all geometry stay in inches. The\nconversion happens only at the display boundary: `mat-units.ts` for the\nfield text, step grid and result strings, and a new optional\n`formatValue` on `useMatCalculator` so the guide-bar cards and dimension\nrows it builds render in the chosen unit. The iOS screen calls the hook\nwithout options, so its behaviour is unchanged (issue #263).\n\nCloses #250\n\n* docs(mat): clarify that board presets are named in inches and shown in cm\n\n* feat(mat): label board presets in centimetres for metric users","tree":{"sha":"4860bab06d96828ac48bd85a3e46289eebbe6432","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/narrowstacks/dorkroom/git/trees/4860bab06d96828ac48bd85a3e46289eebbe6432"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/narrowstacks/dorkroom/git/commits/3a1c9618425e2bb5712efaacf5bd117bfe7dd096","verification":{"payload":"tree 4860bab06d96828ac48bd85a3e46289eebbe6432\nparent 6aeb1da4f9b239a3c3a1359bd5c8e5110e06ed55\nauthor aaron f.a <aaron@affords.art> 1790034387 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790034387 -0700\n\nfeat(mat): follow the global imperial/metric preference (#315)\n\n* feat(mat): follow the global imperial/metric preference\n\nThe mat calculator never read `useMeasurement()`, so a metric user got\ncentimetres on /border and /resize but fractional inches on /mat.\n\nForm state, presets, persistence and all geometry stay in inches. The\nconversion happens only at the display boundary: `mat-units.ts` for the\nfield text, step grid and result strings, and a new optional\n`formatValue` on `useMatCalculator` so the guide-bar cards and dimension\nrows it builds render in the chosen unit. The iOS screen calls the hook\nwithout options, so its behaviour is unchanged (issue #263).\n\nCloses #250\n\n* docs(mat): clarify that board presets are named in inches and shown in cm\n\n* feat(mat): label board presets in centimetres for metric users","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqscHTCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA6HQQACmZp1llXTseb/MsjSbPN9x1\nP3ojMHf1+bUw5KIQ5IYPPLWiV7PwEAG33bJKWVYeU1styNAZxGZMCfc/Ur9Vjx7j\nJxUcN15OU1z0nNkNCIRju3R5ERO3ti1LGIxl5JGJDaXt249nD4z3k0ILT5gN6RBj\nBzuNiC7NeVOaPO2Slk+0QPKfHCcpI7Vg4IKkroG1dN7Az509kONg+u92ZdaHTYCQ\nOWvoYMOFml0fVDaOBPQFbGrVyU162yrrvZcHvaTVAqDh2Y/Ecmkhi8g/ZHZ4Nm7/\nZXCU5ItgY37m+GYgGFCut4lU4687+RUsXl4Fip/OxYbnj+sESgH3M0vhTCIxs/iR