pi.github.com/users/narrowstacks/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/narrowstacks","id":2106980,"login":"narrowstacks","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMDY5ODA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/narrowstacks/dorkroom/commits/24c8754535f6905a267217f6e6182805ef5328c3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T20:45:18Z","email":"aaron@affords.art","name":"aaron f.a"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T20:45:18Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(reciprocity): stop shortening sub-second exposures; share calculator arithmetic (#294)\n\nThe reciprocity power law was implemented in three places, and only one of\nthem guarded the sub-1s region where the law does not hold. For factor > 1\n(every film in RECIPROCITY_FILM_TYPES) raising a fraction to that power\nshrinks it, so the web readout told the photographer to expose for *less*\ntime than they metered:\n\n  Tri-X 400, 1/2s metered -> web said 0.344s, iOS said 0.5s\n  Tri-X 400, 1/4s metered -> web said 0.118s, iOS said 0.25s\n  HP5+,      1/2s metered -> web said 0.403s, iOS said 0.5s\n\nOnly use-reciprocity-calculator.ts had the threshold. The web page''s copy\n(selectReciprocityCalculation) and both chart implementations (the web\nreciprocity-chart-data.ts and the iOS chart-geometry.ts) applied the\nexponent unguarded, so the plotted curve dipped below the identity line\ntoo.\n\nExtract the arithmetic each surface was duplicating into pure modules in\n@dorkroom/logic and route every caller through them:\n\n- applyReciprocity() is now the only place the exponent is applied, so the\n  readout and the curve cannot disagree. calculateReciprocity() builds the\n  whole result from it.\n- calculateResizeExposure() / matchesAspectRatio() replace the resize\n  formulas that the hook and the page each carried, identical down to the\n  .toFixed() calls.\n- calculateExposureAdjustment() replaces the readout assembly both\n  exposure surfaces built from the same three helpers.\n\nTwo behaviours are unified rather than preserved, both toward the tested\nlogic hook:\n\n- An unresolvable reciprocity factor now falls back to 1 (no correction)\n  instead of the web page''s 1.3. A silently-applied guess is\n  indistinguishable from a real film profile.\n- A custom film is labelled ''Custom'' everywhere, matching\n  RECIPROCITY_FILM_TYPES and iOS, rather than the web''s ''Custom profile''.\n\nAdds 24 tests over the new modules, including a sweep asserting that\napplyReciprocity never returns less than the metered time.","tree":{"sha":"f8cb3190c021547145a66bb5811c120cce33f572","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/narrowstacks/dorkroom/git/trees/f8cb3190c021547145a66bb5811c120cce33f572"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/narrowstacks/dorkroom/git/commits/24c8754535f6905a267217f6e6182805ef5328c3","verification":{"payload":"tree f8cb3190c021547145a66bb5811c120cce33f572\nparent f716df96b684ec19def0563d127697b06b278573\nauthor aaron f.a <aaron@affords.art> 1789677918 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789677918 -0700\n\nfix(reciprocity): stop shortening sub-second exposures; share calculator arithmetic (#294)\n\nThe reciprocity power law was implemented in three places, and only one of\nthem guarded the sub-1s region where the law does not hold. For factor > 1\n(every film in RECIPROCITY_FILM_TYPES) raising a fraction to that power\nshrinks it, so the web readout told the photographer to expose for *less*\ntime than they metered:\n\n  Tri-X 400, 1/2s metered -> web said 0.344s, iOS said 0.5s\n  Tri-X 400, 1/4s metered -> web said 0.118s, iOS said 0.25s\n  HP5+,      1/2s metered -> web said 0.403s, iOS said 0.5s\n\nOnly use-reciprocity-calculator.ts had the threshold. The web page''s copy\n(selectReciprocityCalculation) and both chart implementations (the web\nreciprocity-chart-data.ts and the iOS chart-geometry.ts) applied the\nexponent unguarded, so the plotted curve dipped below the identity line\ntoo.\n\nExtract the arithmetic each surface was duplicating into pure modules in\n@dorkroom/logic and route every caller through them:\n\n- applyReciprocity() is now the only place the exponent is applied, so the\n  readout and the curve cannot disagree. calculateReciprocity() builds the\n  whole result from it.\n- calculateResizeExposure() / matchesAspectRatio() replace the resize\n  formulas that the hook and the page each carried, identical down to the\n  .toFixed() calls.\n- calculateExposureAdjustment() replaces the readout assembly both\n  exposure surfaces built from the same three helpers.\n\nTwo behaviours are unified rather than preserved, both toward the tested\nlogic hook:\n\n- An unresolvable reciprocity factor now falls back to 1 (no correction)\n  instead of the web page''s 1.3. A silently-applied guess is\n  indistinguishable from a real film profile.\n- A custom film is labelled ''Custom'' everywhere, matching\n  RECIPROCITY_FILM_TYPES and iOS, rather than the web''s ''Custom profile''.\n\nAdds 24 tests over the new modules, including a sweep asserting that\napplyReciprocity never returns less than the metered time.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqrFFeCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVEgQAAS5QxejeKouvIjk1Jnyz2x0\nBO7xDEvVTIHMs2AO9xslDpYLZExP+KMyPcWyIb9ksI32hCOKpoy1s6+IXB7lVRzM\n6fFOf4fsb8SAx4HRT+lvRYYvSezBYDuytSvDCZ0dyno2EUu8sFi4MLbYRATSrisk\nNghpmtmErkWIITL1zz4RUvabMZxJhwH6yMx9zfY