v2 preset encoding that handles negative offsets natively,\nwith backward-compatible decoding that also repairs corrupted v1 links.\n\nFixes #238","tree":{"sha":"87730320e416960988e62e3d2b811b3bd69bd778","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/narrowstacks/dorkroom/git/trees/87730320e416960988e62e3d2b811b3bd69bd778"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/narrowstacks/dorkroom/git/commits/1d47e1de9716db1e7a5b7bd1a5f8c9e728b48752","verification":{"payload":"tree 87730320e416960988e62e3d2b811b3bd69bd778\nparent d5cdcf515717214775fe545657425a51ae4e5980\nauthor aaron f.a <aaron@affords.art> 1788407445 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788407445 -0700\n\nfix(border): stop preset share links corrupting on negative horizontal offset (#267)\n\nAdds a versioned v2 preset encoding that handles negative offsets natively,\nwith backward-compatible decoding that also repairs corrupted v1 links.\n\nFixes #238","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqmO6VCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAGAAQABFRahBvxl7SegXUS85haVz0\nK1d8gwoYb7Tk2d80q5+8Am0Pb0n8JxyDOX81/qB1J+L8dbwCnIGebHQQlTk27zmD\nbNriixn6wMA5j4X3OMW8QppKww/PtA9z7O1DTBvjn6deCjWRrgKKaAcTPMKASB1m\ntuD3Ldr7kqmT0Q3SeXjOWx15L/NXUZLUdwJBaBm58+oTtfhLAR8xtj94a1spDllK\nQKAd7YD952cXvBkkNu0jSEURghqxmqhNqtyTCAkcDPYHl9Y7gtz9pt/HVwqRy3YO\nDrKI4l0zDck5fJAORpt0GZF0FrX1xe+hBu8/WqomrWpFJgyzj7PQAlvjOaP0BsrK\nXK0693zwafCa2G4BXgXGcwwgW/l6WMAZ3rwI2bVqzMKEbVDh61pp1MiGRQt6R606\nb8VUklMDc0N7ucxiSFu51Qp7SyLxqWyukP96ZEhow0wDCUAEfoubG7vwZjjLd/GG\n+IUGldWy//i5opNuszt/x9zxpm8DDhWXIZHhw0K9sYqqSZVzq6AcMMuxrFuvxvb6\nI3tdzzMMKflJYral7iXIJF0dayddGj8Gyv7md+Q3kmLkMj1bKhAr0CZldhbCBUDc\nwLZhxT1E4qVfAzcMDitpFejD+BDZgLtwG5uGVC5W7BQuu2V+Arh4VRkj8IyXkErt\naWxxsBRxJaaLkJsVqqWI\n=vPGA\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-03T03:50:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/narrowstacks/dorkroom/commit/1d47e1de9716db1e7a5b7bd1a5f8c9e728b48752","node_id":"C_kwDOP0YsJdoAKDFkNDdlMWRlOTcxNmRiMWU3YTViN2JkMWE1ZjhjOWU3MjhiNDg3NTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/narrowstacks/dorkroom/commit/d5cdcf515717214775fe545657425a51ae4e5980","sha":"d5cdcf515717214775fe545657425a51ae4e5980","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/narrowstacks/dorkroom/commits/d5cdcf515717214775fe545657425a51ae4e5980"}],"sha":"1d47e1de9716db1e7a5b7bd1a5f8c9e728b48752","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/narrowstacks/dorkroom/commits/1d47e1de9716db1e7a5b7bd1a5f8c9e728b48752"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2106980?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/narrowstacks","id":2106980,"login":"narrowstacks","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMDY5ODA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/narrowstacks/dorkroom/commits/d5cdcf515717214775fe545657425a51ae4e5980/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-27T02:14:39Z","email":"aaron@affords.art","name":"aaron f.a"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-27T02:14:39Z","email":"aaron@affords.art","name":"aaron f.a"},"message":"fix(scripts): upload PR attachments one per page load\n\nBatch uploads to a PR were losing most of their files. Two independent\ncauses, both confirmed against real PRs:\n\n1. Wrong widget. COMMENT_BOX comma-joined three selectors and took\n   `.first()`, but Playwright resolves `.first()` in DOM order, not\n   selector order. On any PR with inline review threads the loose\n   `textarea[id*=\"comment\"]` arm matched a collapsed inline *reply* box\n   that sits above the main comment box, and `input[type=\"file\"]`\n   `.first()` matched that box''s input too. Files dropped there upload\n   into a widget nobody reads: no placeholder, no error, no URL. On PR\n   #270 this failed 3 out of 3 files. Selectors are now tried in\n   priority order, and the file input is taken from the same\n   <file-attachment> wrapper as the chosen box so the two cannot be\n   mismatched.\n\n2. One upload per page load. The comment box accepts the first upload of\n   a page load and silently swallows every one after it. Measured on PR\n   #268: file A landed in 7s, files B and C produced nothing in 25s each,\n   in any textarea on the page. Every file now gets its own page load.\n   Closing the page also takes any still-in-flight upload with it, so a\n   straggler can never land in the next file''s box.\n\nAttribution no longer guesses. It used to take the first URL in the box\nnot already in a `seen` set, so an out-of-order or late URL silently\npinned the wrong screenshot to the wrong file. The box is now cleared and\nverified empty before each upload, so exactly one URL can be present, and\nGitHub''s own alt text is checked against the filename before the URL is\naccepted.\n\nA single failure no longer discards the run. Files get three attempts\nwith exponential backoff; a genuine GitHub refusal is not retried, since\nretrying a refusal only refuses again. Whatever succeeded is still\nprinted as {path: url} on stdout, failures are listed on stderr with a\nready-to-paste command to retry only those, and the exit code is\nnon-zero. A missing path is likewise one file''s problem, not the run''s.\n\nAlso fixes a latent false positive: the rejection check was /failed/i\nagainst the whole box, so a shot named `light-meter-failed-state.webp`\nread as a GitHub rejection.\n\nThe URL attribution, retry, backoff and failure classification are pure\nexported functions with 27 unit tests in\nscripts/__tests__/github-upload-attachment.test.ts. Verified end to end\nagainst PRs #268, #269, #270 and #272: 3 files in 6.8s with no retries\nwhere the old path took 3m19s, correct per-file URLs confirmed via\nGitHub''s alt text, partial failure returning 3 URLs plus 1 listed failure\nand exit 1, and no comment posted on any PR.","tree":{"sha":"418d1dd4d6eeeaae4398f556316a64fd6d41113d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/narrowstacks/dorkroom/git/trees/418d1dd4d6eeeaae4398f556316a64fd6d41113d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/narrowstacks/dorkroom/git/commits/d5cdcf515717214775fe545657425a51ae4e5980","verification":{"payload":"tree 418d1dd4d6eeeaae4398f556316a64fd6d41113d\nparent f72a668c756a70119896feff4588c79df0cdcddd\nauthor aaron f.a <aaron@affords.art> 1787796879 -0700\ncommitter aaron f.a <aaron@affords.art> 1787796879 -0700\n\nfix(scripts): upload PR attachments one per page load\n\nBatch uploads to a PR were losing most of their files. Two independent\ncauses, both confirmed against real PRs:\n\n1. Wrong widget. COMMENT_BOX comma-joined three selectors and took\n   `.first()`, but Playwright resolves `.first()` in DOM order, not\n   selector order. On any PR with inline review threads the loose\n   `textarea[id*=\"comment\"]` arm matched a collapsed inline *reply* box\n   that sits above the main comment box, and `input[type=\"file\"]`\n   `.first()` matched that box''s input too. Files dropped there upload\n   into a widget nobody reads: no placeholder, no error, no URL. On PR\n   #270 this failed 3 out of 3 files. Selectors are now tried in\n   priority order, and the file input is taken from the same\n   <file-attachment> wrapper as the chosen box so the two cannot be\n   mismatched.\n\n2. One upload per page load. The comment box accepts the first upload of\n   a page load and silently swallows every one after it. Measured on PR\n   #268: file A landed in 7s, files B and C produced nothing in 25s each,\n   in any textarea on the page. Every file now gets its own page load.\n   Closing the page also takes any still-in-flight upload with it, so a\n   straggler can never land in the next file''s box.\n\nAttribution no longer guesses. It used to take the first URL in the box\nnot already in a `seen` set, so an out-of-order or late URL silently\npinned the wrong screenshot to the wrong file. The box is now cleared and\nverified empty before each upload, so exactly one URL can be present, and\nGitHub''s own alt text is checked against the filename before the URL is\naccepted.\n\nA single failure no longer discards the run. Files get three attempts\nwith exponential backoff; a genuine GitHub refusal is not retried, since\nretrying a refusal only refuses again. Whatever succeeded is still\nprinted as {path: url} on stdout, failures are listed on stderr with a\nready-to-paste command to retry only those, and the exit code is\nnon-zero. A missing path is likewise one file''s problem, not the run''s.\n\nAlso fixes a latent false positive: the rejection check was /failed/i\nagainst the whole box, so a shot named `light-meter-failed-state.webp`\nread as a GitHub rejection.\n\nThe URL attribution, retry, backoff and failure classification are pure\nexported functions with 27 unit tests in\nscripts/__tests__/github-upload-attachment.test.ts. Verified end to end\nagainst PRs #268, #269, #270 and #272: 3 files in 6.8s with no retries\nwhere the old path took 3m19s, correct per-file URLs confirmed via\nGitHub''s alt text, partial failure returning 3 URLs plus 1 listed failure\nand exit 1, and no comment posted on any PR.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgSz/gDvtbP0jcgVVEhQC8abOiiw\nyb6IMwcLHm8FgtkfsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQPga0IyF1ZTU1yQxs2Kg7Tl/+9yDtBTxsLBpPOJehStF7VuCW/wgYVoP5wtoGoWGbh\n/ILCBJXXyy6Vbi0tFN8wY=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-27T02:14:48Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2106980?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/narrowstacks","id":2106980,"login":"narrowstacks","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMDY5ODA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/narrowstacks/dorkroom/commit/d5cdcf515717214775fe545657425a51ae4e5980","node_id":"C_kwDOP0YsJdoAKGQ1Y2RjZjUxNTcxNzIxNDc3NWZlNTQ1NjU3NDI1YTUxYWU0ZTU5ODA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/narrowstacks/dorkroom/commit/f72a668c756a70119896feff4588c79df0cdcddd","sha":"f72a668c756a70119896feff4588c79df0cdcddd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/narrowstacks/dorkroom/commits/f72a668c756a70119896feff4588c79df0cdcddd"}],"sha":"d5cdcf515717214775fe545657425a51ae4e5980","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/narrowstacks/dorkroom/commits/d5cdcf515717214775fe545657425a51ae4e5980"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2106980?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/narrowstacks","id":2106980,"login":"narrowstacks","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMDY5ODA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/narrowstacks/dorkroom/commits/f72a668c756a70119896feff4588c79df0cdcddd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-21T08:31:36Z","email":"aaron@affords.art","name":"aaron f.a"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-21T08:31:59Z","email":"aaron@affords.art","name":"aaron f.a"},"message":"docs(claude): resync CLAUDE.md files with the codebase\n\nCorrect claims that drifted, and drop AI-isms (em dashes, curly quotes).\n\n- root: remove the dead docs/search-strategy.md reference and the stale\n  Task-tool search section; list the mobile doc and docs/API.md; widen rule 3\n  to allow published @dorkroom/ui subpath exports; note the docs microfrontend\n- api: document stats/meta/og; /utils lives at the repo root, not api/utils;\n  Supabase routes go through createSupabaseProxy, not withHandler directly\n- ui: shadow-subtle emits no shadow (no --shadow-subtle token); note the\n  data-animations-disabled setting alongside the motion-free themes\n- logic: add constants/ and utils/ to the structure; note the .native.ts split\n- api pkg: document clientId, the per-item Zod filtering, and openapi.ts\n- mobile: screens moved to src/screens with route files as re-exports; tabs\n  are user-pinnable; drop the obsolete text-2xl title note\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FGkAEkc1LEKkiYnLc2hn1d","tree":{"sha":"c2a2608957670d98e1b6953986d19e330d8fa323","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/narrowstacks/dorkroom/git/trees/c2a2608957670d98e1b6953986d19e330d8fa323"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/narrowstacks/dorkroom/git/commits/f72a668c756a70119896feff4588c79df0cdcddd","verification":{"payload":"tree c2a2608957670d98e1b6953986d19e330d8fa323\nparent 7ad146f0e2cceac0cb0ae7150abd0e9ee4c1718b\nauthor aaron f.a <aaron@affords.art> 1787301096 -0700\ncommitter aaron f.a <aaron@affords.art> 1787301119 -0700\n\ndocs(claude): resync CLAUDE.md files with the codebase\n\nCorrect claims that drifted, and drop AI-isms (em dashes, curly quotes).\n\n- root: remove the dead docs/search-strategy.md reference and the stale\n  Task-tool search section; list the mobile doc and docs/API.md; widen rule 3\n  to allow published @dorkroom/ui subpath exports; note the docs microfrontend\n- api: document stats/meta/og; /utils lives at the repo root, not api/utils;\n  Supabase routes go through createSupabaseProxy, not withHandler directly\n- ui: shadow-subtle emits no shadow (no --shadow-subtle token); note the\n  data-animations-disabled setting alongside the motion-free themes\n- logic: add constants/ and utils/ to the structure; note the .native.ts split\n- api pkg: document clientId, the per-item Zod filtering, and openapi.ts\n- mobile: screens moved to src/screens with route files as re-exports; tabs\n  are user-pinnable; drop the obsolete text-2xl title note\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FGkAEkc1LEKkiYnLc2hn1d\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgSz/gDvtbP0jcgVVEhQC8abOiiw\nyb6IMwcLHm8FgtkfsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQLidmyBK8NbIKP9ZPME7qgUEaSYITIqmSvSnVQVs/Rqzm0jSDuvKm0q3vgH3OF9kjf\n6Z7OcC0yhqbPVeolJqXgc=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-21T08:32:04Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2106980?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/narrowstacks","id":2106980,"login":"narrowstacks","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMDY5ODA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/us