te":"2026-08-21T08:19:57Z","email":"41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"github-actions[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-21T08:19:57Z","email":"41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"github-actions[bot]"},"message":"chore: update homepage screenshot [skip ci]","tree":{"sha":"e0de4b6f15f70ea407f4bb78db4b6e94076f8967","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/narrowstacks/dorkroom/git/trees/e0de4b6f15f70ea407f4bb78db4b6e94076f8967"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/narrowstacks/dorkroom/git/commits/7ad146f0e2cceac0cb0ae7150abd0e9ee4c1718b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","id":41898282,"login":"github-actions[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/narrowstacks/dorkroom/commit/7ad146f0e2cceac0cb0ae7150abd0e9ee4c1718b","node_id":"C_kwDOP0YsJdoAKDdhZDE0NmYwZTJjY2VhYzBjYjBhZTcxNTBhYmQwZTllZTRjMTcxOGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/narrowstacks/dorkroom/commit/fec7ff5ec8bfbdbd726605a52eef45c563ada703","sha":"fec7ff5ec8bfbdbd726605a52eef45c563ada703","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/narrowstacks/dorkroom/commits/fec7ff5ec8bfbdbd726605a52eef45c563ada703"}],"sha":"7ad146f0e2cceac0cb0ae7150abd0e9ee4c1718b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/narrowstacks/dorkroom/commits/7ad146f0e2cceac0cb0ae7150abd0e9ee4c1718b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2106980?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/narrowstacks","id":2106980,"login":"narrowstacks","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxMDY5ODA=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/narrowstacks","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/narrowstacks/dorkroom/commits/fec7ff5ec8bfbdbd726605a52eef45c563ada703/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-21T08:18:41Z","email":"aaron@affords.art","name":"aaron f.a"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-21T08:18:41Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(analytics): address Codex review findings from #228 (#234)\n\n* fix(analytics): address Codex review findings from #228\n\nFour issues raised on #228 after it merged.\n\n`search_no_results` fired on every keystroke. Both browse pages debounce\nfiltering by 300ms, so the hook saw a fresh query paired with the previous\nquery''s count; once a search had dead-ended, everything typed on the way to\na query that finds something reported another dead end. Both hooks now\nexpose the debounced query they actually filtered on, and the pages pass\nthat. /development additionally passed `deferredCombinedRows`, which lags a\nfurther render, so it now reads the undeferred rows.\n\n`share_opened` counted bookmarks as shares. The URL parser sets\n`isDirectSelection` for any recipe URL without `source=share`, including the\ncanonical URL of a detail view you opened yourself, so a reload counted as\nopening somebody else''s link and inflated the share/share_opened pair the\nviral coefficient comes from. `InitialUrlState` gains `fromShare`, set only\nfor `source=share`, and the event is gated on it.\n\n`app_error` could carry user-controlled text. The wildcard route matches any\npathname, so a crash while rendering `/person@example.com` put that on the\nwire; bounding it to 255 characters does not make it private.\n`currentRoutePath` is replaced by `currentRouteLabel`, which returns a closed\nunion of the app''s routes or `unknown`. A test pins that list against the\ngenerated route tree so a new route cannot silently fall through to\n`unknown`.\n\n`calculator_used` never reported a border mode. The hook was called without\none, so every border event used `default` and neither `symmetric` nor\n`asymmetric` was ever sent, which is the split those values exist for. The\npage now derives it from the offsets toggle.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FGkAEkc1LEKkiYnLc2hn1d\n\n* feat(scripts): add a scrollTo action to pr-screenshots\n\nA shot is viewport-sized, so a change further down a long page never\nappears in one. The only rendered change in this branch is a single row of\nthe /privacy event table, which sits well below the fold; without this it\ncould not be screenshotted at all.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FGkAEkc1LEKkiYnLc2hn1d\n\n* fix(analytics): wait for a calculator''s mode to settle before reporting it\n\nCodex, on #234: a visitor with offsets stored or a shared preset in the URL\nstill gets `enableOffset === false` on the first render.\n`useLocalStorageFormPersistence` hydrates the form in a mount effect and\n`useUrlPresetLoader` applies the preset in another, both after that render,\nso the effect reported `symmetric` and then `asymmetric` — one visitor,\ntwo events, with the symmetric count absorbing asymmetric users.\n\n/resize has the same shape and has had it since #228: `isEnlargerHeightMode`\nis persisted, so every enlarger-height user was counted under `print_size`\nas well. Fixing it in `useCalculatorAnalytics` covers both, and any later\nsource of a late mode, without each calculator threading a settled signal\nthrough to analytics.\n\nA mode now has to hold for 600ms before it is reported; a change inside the\nwindow cancels the pending report on cleanup. A mode switched to later still\nreports, because the effect re-runs and its own timer fires.\n\n`reportedCalculatorModes()` joins the existing `resetCalculatorAnalytics()`\ntest seam so the new tests can assert what shipped without mocking the wire.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FGkAEkc1LEKkiYnLc2hn1d\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ffcff365dd17dd79ed209d623d2b00607218a6d5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/narrowstacks/dorkroom/git/trees/ffcff365dd17dd79ed209d623d2b00607218a6d5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/narrowstacks/dorkroom/git/commits/fec7ff5ec8bfbdbd726605a52eef45c563ada703","verification":{"payload":"tree ffcff365dd17dd79ed209d623d2b00607218a6d5\nparent 1e641d77b5cbb6781cd54287e4e96eb3b143050f\nauthor aaron f.a <aaron@affords.art> 1787300321 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787300321 -0700\n\nfix(analytics): address Codex review findings from #228 (#234)\n\n* fix(analytics): address Codex review findings from #228\n\nFour issues raised on #228 after it merged.\n\n`search_no_results` fired on every keystroke. Both browse pages debounce\nfiltering by 300ms, so the hook saw a fresh query paired with the previous\nquery''s count; once a search had dead-ended, everything typed on the way to\na query that finds something reported another dead end. Both hooks now\nexpose the debounced query they actually filtered on, and the pages pass\nthat. /development additionally passed `deferredCombinedRows`, which lags a\nfurther render, so it now reads the undeferred rows.\n\n`share_opened` counted bookmarks as shares. The URL parser sets\n`isDirectSelection` for any recipe URL without `source=share`, including the\ncanonical URL of a detail view you opened yourself, so a reload counted as\nopening somebody else''s link and inflated the share/share_opened pair the\nviral coefficient comes from. `InitialUrlState` gains `fromShare`, set only\nfor `source=share`, and the event is gated on it.\n\n`app_error` could carry user-controlled text. The wildcard route matches any\npathname, so a crash while rendering `/person@example.com` put that on the\nwire; bounding it to 255 characters does not make it private.\n`currentRoutePath` is replaced by `currentRouteLabel`, which returns a closed\nunion of the app''s routes or `unknown`. A test pins that list against the\ngenerated route tree so a new route cannot silently fall through to\n`unknown`.\n\n`calculator_used` never reported a border mode. The hook was called without\none, so every border event used `default` and neither `symmetric` nor\n`asymmetric` was ever sent, which is the split those values exist for. The\npage now derives it from the offsets toggle.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FGkAEkc1LEKkiYnLc2hn1d\n\n* feat(scripts): add a scrollTo action to pr-screenshots\n\nA shot is viewport-sized, so a change further down a long page never\nappears in one. The only rendered change in this branch is a single row of\nthe /privacy event table, which sits well below the fold; without this it\ncould not be screenshotted at all.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FGkAEkc1LEKkiYnLc2hn1d\n\n* fix(analytics): wait for a calculator''s mode to settle before reporting it\n\nCodex, on #234: a visitor with offsets stored or a shared preset in the URL\nstill gets `enableOffset === false` on the first render.\n`useLocalStorageFormPersistence` hydrates the form in a mount effect and\n`useUrlPresetLoader` applies the preset in another, both after that render,\nso the effect reported `symmetric` and then `asymmetric` — one visitor,\ntwo events, with the symmetric count absorbing asymmetric users.\n\n/resize has the same shape and has had it since #228: `isEnlargerHeightMode`\nis persisted, so every enlarger-height user was counted under `print_size`\nas well. Fixing it in `useCalculatorAnalytics` covers both, and any later\nsource of a late mode, without each calculator threading a settled signal\nthrough to analytics.\n\nA mode now has to hold for 600ms before it is reported; a change inside the\nwindow cancels the pending report on cleanup. A mode switched to later still\nreports, because the effect re-runs and its own timer fires.\n\n`reportedCalculatorModes()` joins the existing `resetCalculatorAnalytics()`\ntest seam so the new tests can assert what shipped without mocking the wire.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FGkAEkc1LEKkiYnLc2hn1d\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqiAnhCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVrAQAJ3JnsJs627pgcX2SpdsLryI\ntab2eM8bFE0mLyVO1EAqgFmOJYn6UDkFf8VtdJ4Jyh5ZVg1kFX7D3VDx7+93lERw\n/L94hbvO6MC+t/qMrFHhemrLwRG/AbT4jGjCR4YbBRCC3E4bmCTfSZJKWbLE5IWi\nbBbVZxLT2k9WgFhyj7s3OaEOiuHQe8rHlrNwaHm+sLYXxIjwZEwU8KFW0k1X5SPL\n2wHY96/jeZJBhbJcchTPVV2NIH5RzZaGmowejqhjNPvec+Pqd8gAphTALOqg2OTb\ni3S0zKhMxCjBOiyaVu5qS1trnImRn7Dc4lD7hqrFRKHM0NmBpaqEwTlnlsi4pr58\nbpXHQJhg9krzKeDsvigvDdwwf3VxWq3DJvOCQX3gfD0Q7LhEGuiYYmlr7ClG9X1p\nXvht1HK7AbmJp8gI9dsbi0GGNM1ynOaDoNDtfo/npX0p4tQ7xGEaoOf6iUu0GRK1\nsmZlRjvWZKtouGC/25zrAJTE43eUyEs/iv1acI5lkVL/AZwKybX/+kkoNUuP4qC1\n6PHERvjvIB3BM77o6p5h3yyg5rFTS3t00VCUVgK8IOV40E3BOfMAEvpOywhZb7uH\nVEkIDENBwD4MvJSL9f2OmjOydFjyTOlyF19jEtSBJFVe1WglfbP3h6y4nrw2l3Tt\nl2PWX+jZXxCDXlAt2gLj\n=g/CZ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-21T08:18:42Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/narrowstacks/dorkroom/commit/fec7ff5ec8bfbdbd726605a52eef45c563ada703","n